1
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:33,116
Hm.

2
00:00:33,908 --> 00:00:34,909
What's the matter?

3
00:00:36,119 --> 00:00:38,038
It's your eyes.

4
00:00:39,914 --> 00:00:42,500
It's the same color as your eyes.

5
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:49,632
The way I felt when I saw this…

6
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,635
This feeling…

7
00:00:56,181 --> 00:00:57,515
What is it called?

8
00:01:32,342 --> 00:01:34,219
"Major Gilbert.

9
00:01:34,302 --> 00:01:37,180
I've been in the hospital
for 120 days now.

10
00:01:37,889 --> 00:01:39,682
My strength has almost recovered.

11
00:01:39,766 --> 00:01:42,477
Movement is still a little difficult

12
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,521
but I can perform my duties.

13
00:01:44,604 --> 00:01:46,523
Please let me return to my post soon."

14
00:02:48,668 --> 00:02:49,669
KINGDOM OF ENCIEL
SOMEWHERE IN THE CAPITAL OF ENCHAINE

15
00:02:49,752 --> 00:02:52,505
Her existence
had been kept hidden from everyone.

16
00:02:53,214 --> 00:02:56,134
However, some of the people
who knew about her

17
00:02:56,217 --> 00:02:58,219
said that she was a weapon.

18
00:02:58,970 --> 00:03:01,264
She would fight if you ordered her to.

19
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,391
She just looked like a human.

20
00:03:04,058 --> 00:03:05,476
She was just a tool…

21
00:03:06,060 --> 00:03:07,478
without a heart.

22
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:12,358
Lieutenant Hodgins?

23
00:03:12,442 --> 00:03:13,860
This way.

24
00:03:14,360 --> 00:03:15,737
Uh? Oh.

25
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:20,825
Yeah. Sorry.

26
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:25,079
Violet!

27
00:03:26,206 --> 00:03:27,248
Are you okay?

28
00:03:27,999 --> 00:03:29,083
Are you hurt?

29
00:03:33,671 --> 00:03:34,881
The major?

30
00:03:35,632 --> 00:03:37,091
Where's Major Gilbert?

31
00:03:38,301 --> 00:03:39,761
He's, uh, not here.

32
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:41,763
Where is he?

33
00:03:42,847 --> 00:03:44,849
Did he return home already?

34
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:47,727
How are his injuries doing anyway?

35
00:03:48,269 --> 00:03:50,271
I know they were pretty severe.

36
00:03:51,064 --> 00:03:52,148
Tell me.

37
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:56,361
Is the major actually… alive?

38
00:03:58,905 --> 00:03:59,781
Well, he's…

39
00:03:59,864 --> 00:04:02,659
You're being discharged from the hospital.

40
00:04:02,742 --> 00:04:05,912
Lieutenant Hodgins came all this way
to pick you up, you know.

41
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:10,458
Uh, yeah, that's right.

42
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:12,168
Excuse me.

43
00:04:12,252 --> 00:04:13,461
Lieutenant Hodgins.

44
00:04:14,045 --> 00:04:17,048
Violet. Relax.

45
00:04:17,131 --> 00:04:19,550
I had forgotten
that you were a Lieutenant.

46
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:22,679
-I apologize, sir.
-It's okay.

47
00:04:22,762 --> 00:04:24,305
Here. Sit down.

48
00:04:25,848 --> 00:04:26,683
Anyway…

49
00:04:27,267 --> 00:04:29,602
I was wondering
if you actually remember me.

50
00:04:30,144 --> 00:04:32,021
Yes. We have met twice before.

51
00:04:32,105 --> 00:04:34,941
During the training
and the night before the battle.

52
00:04:35,024 --> 00:04:36,818
Yeah. You are right.

53
00:04:38,861 --> 00:04:41,030
What were you doing?

54
00:04:41,114 --> 00:04:44,534
I was writing a report
to Major Gilbert.

55
00:04:44,617 --> 00:04:46,286
They said that writing words down

56
00:04:46,369 --> 00:04:48,621
would help to improve my condition
a great deal.

57
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:51,332
So, how is the major?

58
00:04:59,590 --> 00:05:01,134
Don't worry, Violet.

59
00:05:02,218 --> 00:05:05,263
He's the one who asked me
to come here for you.

60
00:05:10,184 --> 00:05:12,437
So then, that means that he's fine.

61
00:05:14,230 --> 00:05:16,649
The doctor told me
that we won the war.

62
00:05:17,734 --> 00:05:19,902
What post is he assigned to now?

63
00:05:20,486 --> 00:05:22,447
When will I be able to join him?

64
00:05:23,948 --> 00:05:25,950
First, get changed.

65
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:28,119
I'll have them
send the car in the meantime.

66
00:05:30,621 --> 00:05:33,374
These finally arrived.
These are your belongings.

67
00:05:36,252 --> 00:05:40,590
It looks like they delivered it
to an army base far away by mistake.

68
00:05:41,716 --> 00:05:42,550
The brooch.

69
00:05:42,633 --> 00:05:43,468
Huh?

70
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,762
Where is the emerald brooch?

71
00:05:45,845 --> 00:05:46,971
Huh?

72
00:05:47,055 --> 00:05:49,015
This is everything there was
from the garrison

73
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:50,767
in the place where they found you.

74
00:05:52,352 --> 00:05:54,062
If it's not here, I have to look for it.

75
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:55,521
Violet!

76
00:05:55,605 --> 00:05:56,981
Someone gave it to me.

77
00:05:58,024 --> 00:05:59,734
The major gave it to me!

78
00:06:05,114 --> 00:06:06,157
I understand.

79
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:08,159
I'll be sure to look for it.

80
00:06:08,826 --> 00:06:10,244
Don't worry.

81
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:12,038
-Yes, but--
-Anyway…

82
00:06:12,747 --> 00:06:14,374
You come along with me now.

83
00:06:15,124 --> 00:06:16,959
Those are his direct orders.

84
00:06:19,295 --> 00:06:20,171
Orders?

85
00:06:22,256 --> 00:06:23,383
I understand.

86
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:29,806
Lieutenant?

87
00:06:29,889 --> 00:06:33,518
When am I going to receive
my next orders from the major?

88
00:06:33,601 --> 00:06:35,561
It's just that in my current condition,

89
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:38,231
the duties I'm capable of performing
are limited.

90
00:06:39,399 --> 00:06:40,441
Violet.

91
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:42,193
I brought you a gift.

92
00:06:42,276 --> 00:06:44,946
I didn't really know what you'd like,
so I bought three.

93
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:46,447
What do you think?

94
00:06:46,531 --> 00:06:47,698
I don't need them.

95
00:06:48,324 --> 00:06:49,158
Uh…

96
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:51,202
No. You have to choose one.

97
00:06:51,285 --> 00:06:53,371
So pretend that the world
is about to end, okay?

98
00:06:53,454 --> 00:06:54,747
Three, two…

99
00:06:54,831 --> 00:06:56,040
Then, the puppy.

100
00:06:56,124 --> 00:06:57,250
Here.

101
00:07:08,511 --> 00:07:10,680
Why did you choose the puppy?

102
00:07:12,807 --> 00:07:15,226
Because the major's brother once told me,

103
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:17,270
"You're actually just like Gilbert's dog."

104
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:22,692
Looks like it's gonna be a long journey.

105
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:26,612
The train tracks around here
were damaged during the bombing

106
00:07:26,696 --> 00:07:28,114
and aren't usable anymore.

107
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:30,450
Have you ever been to Leiden before?

108
00:07:31,492 --> 00:07:32,577
No.

109
00:07:34,162 --> 00:07:36,080
Gilbert was thinking all along

110
00:07:36,164 --> 00:07:39,625
about what your future would hold
after the war.

111
00:07:40,460 --> 00:07:42,503
That's why he was saying
that he wants to leave you

112
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:45,006
with the folks
at the Evergarden household,

113
00:07:45,089 --> 00:07:47,008
his most trusted relatives.

114
00:07:51,512 --> 00:07:54,015
I contacted them earlier,

115
00:07:54,098 --> 00:07:56,100
and they'd be more than happy
to take you in.

116
00:07:56,184 --> 00:07:58,144
I'm taking you there to meet them now.

117
00:08:06,652 --> 00:08:08,070
Thank you for coming.

118
00:08:09,405 --> 00:08:10,907
This is Violet.

119
00:08:11,407 --> 00:08:14,327
And this is the lady
of the Evergarden household.

120
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,579
You can say hello.

121
00:08:18,206 --> 00:08:20,500
Oh, a bow would be good enough.

122
00:08:21,125 --> 00:08:24,545
Doesn't it take
around three days from Enchaine now?

123
00:08:24,629 --> 00:08:27,715
Yes. Normally,
I'd be able to return in one day.

124
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:31,093
But the war went on
for four years.

125
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:33,888
It's going to take some more time
to restore everything.

126
00:08:35,181 --> 00:08:36,724
Well, Violet dear.

127
00:08:37,308 --> 00:08:38,684
Please, have a drink.

128
00:08:43,439 --> 00:08:45,983
I'm sorry! Don't force yourself!

129
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:49,320
Oh, no! You'll get burned.

130
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:53,074
It's not a problem.
I'm not able to feel the heat.

131
00:08:53,157 --> 00:08:54,700
But your bandages…

132
00:08:54,784 --> 00:08:57,453
We have to cool them down quickly.
Oliver, bring some ice!

133
00:08:57,537 --> 00:08:58,663
Yes, madam.

134
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:03,709
These arms are made
of adamant silver.

135
00:09:04,335 --> 00:09:06,462
They're a bit clumsy, but they're sturdy.

136
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:07,964
I'm not used to them yet.

137
00:09:08,047 --> 00:09:11,217
Someday, I'll be able to use them
with no problem, though.

138
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:18,432
Can you come this way
for a minute?

139
00:09:19,892 --> 00:09:22,853
I used these gloves when I was younger.

140
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:25,940
Those are quite nice. Try them on.

141
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:31,779
Yeah. They look good on you.

142
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,281
They do.

143
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:37,785
Well, I'm going to get going now.

144
00:09:38,411 --> 00:09:40,079
I have to get back
to the office.

145
00:09:40,663 --> 00:09:41,622
Oh.

146
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:42,915
Violet.

147
00:09:43,708 --> 00:09:46,586
Be sure to listen closely to Tiffany.

148
00:09:46,669 --> 00:09:47,837
It's okay.

149
00:09:47,920 --> 00:09:50,590
You don't have to worry about us at all.

150
00:09:50,673 --> 00:09:52,925
Think of me as your real mother, dear.

151
00:09:53,009 --> 00:09:55,094
You can tell me anything. Okay?

152
00:09:57,597 --> 00:09:58,973
Yes, but I…

153
00:10:00,016 --> 00:10:03,269
don't have any parents,
so I don't need replacements.

154
00:10:05,104 --> 00:10:06,522
Don't say that, dear.

155
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:11,277
I had a son,
but he was killed in the war.

156
00:10:13,112 --> 00:10:16,032
I can't become
a replacement for your lost child.

157
00:10:16,115 --> 00:10:17,158
I, uh…

158
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:19,035
Okay, listen, Violet.

159
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:23,539
It's Gilbert's wish for you
to live happily here.

160
00:10:24,206 --> 00:10:25,041
So…

161
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:27,043
do you understand?

162
00:10:41,223 --> 00:10:42,683
The major!

163
00:10:43,309 --> 00:10:46,520
Major Gilbert. Why is he leaving me here?

164
00:10:47,438 --> 00:10:51,150
Is it because I lost my arms,
and lost my value as a weapon?

165
00:10:51,942 --> 00:10:55,029
If I just trained a little,
I'd still be able to fight!

166
00:10:56,864 --> 00:10:58,032
Violet, you know that…

167
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:00,284
Well, you know the war is over.

168
00:11:01,869 --> 00:11:03,579
I am the major's tool.

169
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:06,540
But if he doesn't need me anymore,

170
00:11:07,166 --> 00:11:08,501
then I should be discarded.

171
00:11:10,419 --> 00:11:11,379
Please do it.

172
00:11:13,089 --> 00:11:15,049
Please discard me somewhere.

173
00:11:20,388 --> 00:11:21,806
Lieutenant Hodgins.

174
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:24,141
Oh, I forgot to tell you.

175
00:11:24,225 --> 00:11:27,561
I left the army.
I'm not a Lieutenant anymore.

176
00:11:28,312 --> 00:11:29,814
Then what should I call you?

177
00:11:30,398 --> 00:11:31,899
Call me "President."

178
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:35,903
This is my company.

179
00:11:37,780 --> 00:11:41,033
I bought an old house
and renovated it a bit.

180
00:11:41,867 --> 00:11:44,161
The first floor has the reception desk.

181
00:11:45,371 --> 00:11:46,414
All right, sir.

182
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:48,374
If I could ask you to please write down

183
00:11:48,457 --> 00:11:50,793
the receiver's and sender's addresses
on this form here.

184
00:11:50,876 --> 00:11:52,628
And we ask you to please allow

185
00:11:52,712 --> 00:11:54,797
at least three days
for it to be delivered.

186
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:57,967
The second floor houses
the office and the writing department.

187
00:11:58,050 --> 00:11:59,802
-Writing?
-Yes.

188
00:12:00,386 --> 00:12:03,723
This department writes letters
at the requests of our clients.

189
00:12:04,557 --> 00:12:07,268
There are still many people
who don't know how to write.

190
00:12:08,394 --> 00:12:10,020
I didn't know how to write either

191
00:12:10,604 --> 00:12:12,314
until the major taught me how.

192
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:15,067
I see.

193
00:12:17,278 --> 00:12:20,489
I was thinking about starting
a business once the war ended.

194
00:12:20,573 --> 00:12:23,868
The government's postal service
doesn't address the needs of civilians,

195
00:12:23,951 --> 00:12:26,078
so, I thought it would be
a good opportunity.

196
00:12:27,246 --> 00:12:29,039
Now, here's your orders…

197
00:12:29,832 --> 00:12:31,542
Violet Evergarden.

198
00:12:32,209 --> 00:12:34,420
The fact is,
that Gilbert left you in my care.

199
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:37,548
So, I'm going to give you orders
in his place.

200
00:12:38,257 --> 00:12:40,050
You're still very useful, Violet.

201
00:12:40,760 --> 00:12:42,970
You can work. Right here.

202
00:12:46,098 --> 00:12:47,057
Benedict.

203
00:12:47,725 --> 00:12:49,226
Yeah, what's up, President?

204
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:52,062
You're supposed to say
"How can I help you, President?"

205
00:12:52,646 --> 00:12:53,564
So, what's up?

206
00:12:53,647 --> 00:12:55,524
Ow! Why'd you do that?

207
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:56,942
You didn't listen to me.

208
00:12:57,026 --> 00:12:59,570
This is Benedict. He's a postman here.

209
00:13:00,154 --> 00:13:02,948
He's an old friend
from before I started this company.

210
00:13:03,032 --> 00:13:05,409
And, Benedict,
let me introduce you to Violet.

211
00:13:08,746 --> 00:13:10,873
She'll be a postman. Starting today.

212
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,042
She's just a little kid.

213
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:15,961
She's highly capable
of performing her duties.

214
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:18,547
I'm going to go to the bank for a bit.

215
00:13:18,631 --> 00:13:20,716
Teach her what she needs to know.

216
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:24,512
Put your stuff in here.

217
00:13:24,595 --> 00:13:25,679
Yes, sir.

218
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:26,889
Your uniform.

219
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:29,558
-Put it on.
-Yes, of course, sir.

220
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:34,063
Sort them just like it says here.
Then put them in those shelves over there.

221
00:13:34,688 --> 00:13:38,192
There's a huge pile of mail,
but you don't have to rush.

222
00:13:39,527 --> 00:13:41,445
And the break room is on the second floor.

223
00:13:42,071 --> 00:13:43,197
I understand, sir.

224
00:13:45,324 --> 00:13:46,325
See you.

225
00:14:04,593 --> 00:14:07,263
Sir. I've almost completed my duties.

226
00:14:07,346 --> 00:14:08,722
Were you working the whole time?

227
00:14:08,806 --> 00:14:10,266
Without taking a break?

228
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:12,601
I'm used to long operations.

229
00:14:14,854 --> 00:14:19,525
So, uh, you maybe want to try
delivering the mail?

230
00:14:19,608 --> 00:14:20,860
Delivering?

231
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:24,363
You deliver the letter
to the address that's written on it.

232
00:14:29,326 --> 00:14:31,495
Anyway, I'm going to go home now.

233
00:14:34,874 --> 00:14:35,708
See you tomorrow.

234
00:14:38,168 --> 00:14:39,420
Violet!

235
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:44,383
What are you doing?

236
00:14:45,050 --> 00:14:46,176
Delivering the mail.

237
00:14:48,679 --> 00:14:51,557
Uh, I meant
you can deliver the mail tomorrow.

238
00:14:52,516 --> 00:14:55,561
And make sure
to take breaks during work.

239
00:14:55,644 --> 00:14:57,938
You just got out
of the hospital after all.

240
00:14:58,022 --> 00:14:59,106
It's not a problem.

241
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:02,401
All right, you know what? It is a problem.

242
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:06,572
Now listen, Violet. Go ahead and eat.

243
00:15:09,575 --> 00:15:10,618
Yes, sir.

244
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:14,622
You can return to the office
after you eat.

245
00:15:15,456 --> 00:15:18,626
We only have space in the attic,
but you can sleep there.

246
00:15:19,710 --> 00:15:23,797
Uh, the Evergardens have agreed
to take you in

247
00:15:23,881 --> 00:15:25,633
and have you live with them

248
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:27,468
until you become an adult.

249
00:15:28,218 --> 00:15:30,888
But it looks like leaving you
at the mansion…

250
00:15:31,972 --> 00:15:33,265
Yeah, that's a problem.

251
00:15:33,807 --> 00:15:36,226
-Ow!
-Hey! I was trying to put it nicely!

252
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:38,228
How was I supposed to know?

253
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:40,606
Well, see you tomorrow.

254
00:15:43,776 --> 00:15:44,735
I'll walk you.

255
00:15:47,196 --> 00:15:50,950
So, what was the last order
you received from Gilbert?

256
00:15:51,700 --> 00:15:54,328
He said,
"You have to live and be free."

257
00:15:56,246 --> 00:15:58,123
And, I, uh…

258
00:16:02,044 --> 00:16:06,006
You've been in the army
ever since you were a child.

259
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:08,592
You've spent your life
fulfilling your duties.

260
00:16:09,259 --> 00:16:12,763
However, you're going to learn
many things in the future.

261
00:16:14,974 --> 00:16:17,351
Although, it might be easier

262
00:16:17,434 --> 00:16:19,979
to keep living if you never learn them.

263
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:27,528
You see, you don't realize yet,
but your body is on fire

264
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:29,822
and burning up
because of the things you did.

265
00:16:32,574 --> 00:16:33,993
I'm not burning.

266
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:35,494
Yes, you are.

267
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:36,954
I'm not burning.

268
00:16:37,037 --> 00:16:38,831
-I don't get it.
-No.

269
00:16:39,581 --> 00:16:40,749
You are burning.

270
00:16:43,544 --> 00:16:46,964
I saw you like that, and left you alone.

271
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:51,010
That's why when Gilbert left you with me,

272
00:16:51,093 --> 00:16:52,803
it was my chance for redemption.

273
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:56,682
Someday, you'll understand what I said.

274
00:16:57,349 --> 00:17:01,562
And then you'll realize for the first time
that you have many burns.

275
00:17:25,836 --> 00:17:27,171
Uh, Ms. Doll?

276
00:17:27,254 --> 00:17:29,757
Uh, no, my name is Violet.

277
00:17:29,840 --> 00:17:32,634
Well, in that case, Miss Violet,

278
00:17:32,718 --> 00:17:34,762
can I get you to write something for me?

279
00:17:35,679 --> 00:17:36,513
Write for…

280
00:17:39,850 --> 00:17:41,018
"You were the first person…

281
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:43,479
…the first person
who was kind to me.

282
00:17:43,562 --> 00:17:45,439
I appreciated it.

283
00:17:47,357 --> 00:17:49,109
You were everything to me.

284
00:17:52,362 --> 00:17:54,782
I would have done anything for you.

285
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:56,366
Anything at all."

286
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:57,951
Go!

287
00:18:01,997 --> 00:18:03,874
"I want to know how you feel.

288
00:18:05,542 --> 00:18:07,961
I want to understand what's in your heart.

289
00:18:11,256 --> 00:18:14,760
Even though we're apart now…

290
00:18:17,012 --> 00:18:18,430
I love you."

291
00:18:22,309 --> 00:18:23,352
We'll end with that.

292
00:18:23,435 --> 00:18:25,479
Okay? What do you think?

293
00:18:26,563 --> 00:18:27,397
Great!

294
00:18:29,608 --> 00:18:30,901
"I love you."

295
00:18:34,071 --> 00:18:37,741
Please drop by at the reception
desk on the first floor for delivery.

296
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:40,077
Sir.

297
00:18:41,411 --> 00:18:44,039
All of us here
at the Auto Memories Doll Service…

298
00:18:44,873 --> 00:18:47,000
wish to thank you for coming in today.

299
00:18:54,842 --> 00:18:57,219
So, who are you?

300
00:19:02,141 --> 00:19:04,017
I don't understand how you knew.

301
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:04,977
Huh?

302
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:08,856
How did you know
that the man just now…

303
00:19:09,523 --> 00:19:11,150
wanted to say "I love you"?

304
00:19:13,735 --> 00:19:15,988
Do you want to work
as an Auto Memories Doll?

305
00:19:16,864 --> 00:19:20,450
Yes. It's still hard for me to hold a pen.

306
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:22,369
But I can operate a typewriter.

307
00:19:23,078 --> 00:19:25,164
No, that's not what I mean.

308
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:26,999
I wanted to ask you why.

309
00:19:27,082 --> 00:19:28,125
I just want to know!

310
00:19:32,296 --> 00:19:33,338
"I love you."

311
00:19:34,631 --> 00:19:36,133
What does it mean?

312
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:43,599
The major said those words to me
after he gave me my last orders.

313
00:19:44,641 --> 00:19:48,478
That was the first time
I heard those words from the major.

314
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:52,482
I just don't understand
what that really means.

315
00:19:52,566 --> 00:19:57,154
So, I thought this might… help me learn.

316
00:19:59,323 --> 00:20:00,449
Normally,

317
00:20:00,532 --> 00:20:04,828
people become Auto Memories Dolls
because they do understand that.

318
00:20:05,662 --> 00:20:06,622
But…

319
00:20:07,289 --> 00:20:08,582
It's okay.

320
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:18,008
She had always just followed
Gilbert's orders in the past.

321
00:20:19,009 --> 00:20:21,136
That was the first time
she asserted her own will.

322
00:20:22,346 --> 00:20:24,014
Everyone said she didn't have a heart

323
00:20:24,723 --> 00:20:27,851
but she said, "I want to know
what 'I love you' means."

324
00:20:33,982 --> 00:20:37,444
No way! There's no way
I'm going to let you die!

325
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:42,866
Stop it.

326
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:47,788
Stop it already!

327
00:20:53,377 --> 00:20:54,419
Enough.

328
00:20:58,882 --> 00:21:00,550
Now, Violet, listen.

329
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:04,137
You have to live…

330
00:21:04,972 --> 00:21:06,473
and be free.

331
00:21:12,729 --> 00:21:14,022
I mean it.

332
00:21:19,987 --> 00:21:21,655
I love you.

333
00:21:21,738 --> 00:21:24,157
I LOVE YOU AND THE AUTO MEMORY DOLL

334
00:21:26,368 --> 00:21:31,123
FOUR YEARS AGO

335
00:21:31,206 --> 00:21:33,125
Hey. Get up.

336
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:43,427
I found her
in the northeastern war zone.

337
00:21:46,805 --> 00:21:47,848
Her name is…

338
00:21:48,515 --> 00:21:50,183
Violet Evergarden.

339
00:21:50,767 --> 00:21:52,227
She's going to work
as an apprentice

340
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:54,813
Auto Memories Doll starting today.

341
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:58,817
Please teach her
whatever you can about the job.

342
00:21:58,900 --> 00:21:59,901
Okay.

343
00:22:00,402 --> 00:22:03,322
Um, first off… Hmm.

344
00:22:03,905 --> 00:22:07,075
How much do you know about
what Auto Memories Dolls do?

345
00:22:07,659 --> 00:22:11,330
I know that they write letters
at the request of other people.

346
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:13,832
Lieutenant Hodgins… I mean,

347
00:22:13,915 --> 00:22:15,792
the president told me so.

348
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:17,294
Yes, that's right.

349
00:22:17,878 --> 00:22:22,090
I can't say that I completely understand,
but I think I can perform my duties.

350
00:22:23,091 --> 00:22:27,220
It's not that easy! "Duties?"
What are you even talking about?

351
00:22:27,304 --> 00:22:30,349
Iris, that's enough. Get back to work.

352
00:22:31,433 --> 00:22:32,559
Fine.

353
00:22:34,102 --> 00:22:38,357
Oh, that reminds me, I haven't introduced
the other Dolls to you yet.

354
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:39,524
You see, "Doll" refers to--

355
00:22:39,608 --> 00:22:41,860
It's an abbreviation
for Auto Memories Doll.

356
00:22:41,943 --> 00:22:43,653
I figured it out the other day.

357
00:22:43,737 --> 00:22:45,072
Right again.

358
00:22:45,655 --> 00:22:48,033
The girl just now… Her name is Iris.

359
00:22:48,116 --> 00:22:50,911
She's a new hire
who just completed her training course.

360
00:22:50,994 --> 00:22:52,454
And that's Erica.

361
00:22:52,537 --> 00:22:55,082
She and I have both been working
as Dolls for a while.

362
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:57,042
You'll meet the others soon.

363
00:22:57,125 --> 00:22:59,419
This company is still pretty young,

364
00:22:59,503 --> 00:23:01,797
so, we're all kinda like rookies here.

365
00:23:02,381 --> 00:23:05,675
Violet, do you know how to use
a typewriter by any chance?

366
00:23:06,551 --> 00:23:08,178
I've never used one before.

367
00:23:08,762 --> 00:23:11,681
Then why don't you start off
by practicing typing?

368
00:23:11,765 --> 00:23:13,892
How can she become a Doll like this?

369
00:23:13,975 --> 00:23:16,895
Iris, can we borrow your manual?

370
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:18,397
Yeah!

371
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:24,069
So, uh, sit down.

372
00:23:24,653 --> 00:23:25,529
Understood, ma'am.

373
00:23:25,612 --> 00:23:26,655
Oh.

374
00:23:31,868 --> 00:23:32,744
Oh.

375
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:34,746
It's better to take off your gloves.

376
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:35,997
Okay.

377
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:44,256
Are you okay?

378
00:23:45,632 --> 00:23:46,800
It's not a problem.

379
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:51,304
Oh, then why don't you try it out a bit?

380
00:23:52,514 --> 00:23:54,766
Set the paper like this.

381
00:23:54,850 --> 00:23:56,560
Turn the knob and feed it in.

382
00:23:56,643 --> 00:23:59,312
Place your pointer fingers
on these keys here

383
00:23:59,396 --> 00:24:01,148
and try typing something.

384
00:24:01,231 --> 00:24:02,065
Okay.

385
00:24:09,364 --> 00:24:11,450
That's right. Just like that.

386
00:24:12,909 --> 00:24:16,204
Now, just remember where your fingers
should go for the different letters.

387
00:24:16,788 --> 00:24:19,458
Let's try typing
what it says in this manual. Oh?

388
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:49,321
Oh, wait. Violet.

389
00:24:54,826 --> 00:24:56,328
Violet! Stop!

390
00:24:59,748 --> 00:25:00,874
Uh…

391
00:25:02,584 --> 00:25:03,960
Do it a little more…

392
00:25:05,170 --> 00:25:07,172
quietly. Okay?

393
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:10,592
I'm done!

394
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:12,802
How is this?

395
00:25:15,639 --> 00:25:18,058
Mm. All right then, Violet, let's see.

396
00:25:18,975 --> 00:25:19,809
Yes.

397
00:25:26,107 --> 00:25:26,942
Hm.

398
00:25:27,651 --> 00:25:31,613
It looks good on you.
My opinion was right after all.

399
00:25:33,031 --> 00:25:35,700
Oh, and don't forget this.

400
00:25:36,618 --> 00:25:37,744
Sorry for being late.

401
00:25:40,288 --> 00:25:41,373
You can open it.

402
00:25:43,416 --> 00:25:44,251
All right, then.

403
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:49,548
This is…

404
00:25:49,631 --> 00:25:51,883
This is the brooch that the major gave me!

405
00:25:52,467 --> 00:25:54,386
It was on the black market.

406
00:25:54,469 --> 00:25:57,264
Someone must have stolen it
from your belongings.

407
00:26:04,938 --> 00:26:07,274
So then, Violet,

408
00:26:07,357 --> 00:26:10,068
do you want to attend
one of the Doll training courses?

409
00:26:10,151 --> 00:26:11,778
They have short-term courses, too.

410
00:26:12,320 --> 00:26:14,239
Iris attended one a while ago.

411
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:16,032
Yeah, but the teacher is really strict.

412
00:26:17,200 --> 00:26:18,952
I think it'll be good for you.

413
00:26:40,640 --> 00:26:42,642
Leiden is such a big city!

414
00:26:42,726 --> 00:26:44,019
Yeah, I know.

415
00:26:44,102 --> 00:26:48,148
I got lost because it has so many
more roads than where I'm from.

416
00:26:48,231 --> 00:26:51,901
They say it's easier
to find a job if you received a brooch.

417
00:26:51,985 --> 00:26:54,613
I just want to graduate and then go home.

418
00:26:54,696 --> 00:26:56,156
I bet you just want the brooch.

419
00:26:58,241 --> 00:26:59,159
I guess.

420
00:27:00,702 --> 00:27:01,536
Quiet.

421
00:27:01,620 --> 00:27:02,537
Oh? Oh.

422
00:27:11,921 --> 00:27:12,839
Hmm.

423
00:27:13,757 --> 00:27:15,759
I would like to welcome all of you

424
00:27:15,842 --> 00:27:18,345
to the Auto Memories Doll Training School.

425
00:27:20,055 --> 00:27:21,306
I'm very sorry.

426
00:27:21,848 --> 00:27:24,684
You will be marked absent
on your second tardy.

427
00:27:24,768 --> 00:27:25,602
Yes, ma'am.

428
00:27:27,437 --> 00:27:29,230
Now that the war is over,

429
00:27:29,314 --> 00:27:31,858
the demand for Dolls
has never been higher.

430
00:27:31,941 --> 00:27:34,277
Of course, it is possible to become a Doll

431
00:27:34,361 --> 00:27:35,904
without attending our school.

432
00:27:35,987 --> 00:27:40,158
But our objective
is not to train just another Doll.

433
00:27:40,241 --> 00:27:42,911
It is to train you to become
the best Doll you can be.

434
00:27:43,453 --> 00:27:46,498
Graduating from our school
is proof of excellence.

435
00:27:47,582 --> 00:27:50,502
However, if I do not deem you
a worthy Doll,

436
00:27:50,585 --> 00:27:53,088
you will never be given this symbol.

437
00:27:54,964 --> 00:27:56,424
Are you prepared to begin?

438
00:27:57,550 --> 00:27:58,843
Affirmative, ma'am.

439
00:27:59,969 --> 00:28:01,596
A qualified Doll

440
00:28:01,680 --> 00:28:05,141
must be able to type
as fast as someone is speaking.

441
00:28:05,725 --> 00:28:07,602
Now, you may begin.

442
00:28:12,857 --> 00:28:15,485
Is something wrong,
Ms. Evergarden?

443
00:28:15,568 --> 00:28:17,070
You did not specify a speed.

444
00:28:19,572 --> 00:28:20,615
I see.

445
00:28:21,324 --> 00:28:23,451
Then you can type if it's specified?

446
00:28:23,952 --> 00:28:26,705
All right, 200 characters per minute.

447
00:28:26,788 --> 00:28:28,081
Affirmative.

448
00:28:34,170 --> 00:28:36,548
-I'll begin.
-Very well.

449
00:28:45,306 --> 00:28:48,977
The letter-writing skills
an admirable Doll must have

450
00:28:49,060 --> 00:28:52,397
includes knowledge of grammar, vocabulary,

451
00:28:52,480 --> 00:28:54,983
and several forms and styles for letters.

452
00:28:56,443 --> 00:28:57,318
Time is up.

453
00:28:59,320 --> 00:29:01,948
Now, I shall announce
your evaluations for today.

454
00:29:02,532 --> 00:29:04,576
Grammar results. Full marks.

455
00:29:04,659 --> 00:29:06,745
Violet Evergarden.

456
00:29:06,828 --> 00:29:09,622
Vocabulary results. Full marks.

457
00:29:09,706 --> 00:29:11,124
Violet Evergarden.

458
00:29:13,543 --> 00:29:15,003
In today's class,

459
00:29:15,086 --> 00:29:18,590
we will be training to write
on another's behalf.

460
00:29:18,673 --> 00:29:22,177
-Are you ready?
-Let us do our best, Ms. Luculia.

461
00:29:22,260 --> 00:29:24,262
So, who do you want to address it to?

462
00:29:25,221 --> 00:29:26,139
Hm?

463
00:29:27,223 --> 00:29:29,893
By that, do you mean,
someone I'd like to write to?

464
00:29:31,728 --> 00:29:33,480
Just choose someone close to you,

465
00:29:33,563 --> 00:29:35,690
who you'd like
to express your feelings to.

466
00:29:36,775 --> 00:29:38,234
Someone I'm close to?

467
00:29:40,195 --> 00:29:42,989
Please address it to Mr. Claudia Hodgins.

468
00:29:43,072 --> 00:29:46,242
Claudia? Is that a friend? Family?

469
00:29:46,326 --> 00:29:47,827
He's my boss.

470
00:29:50,330 --> 00:29:53,124
That is all. I am concluding my report.

471
00:29:53,208 --> 00:29:55,126
Violet Evergarden.

472
00:29:55,210 --> 00:29:57,378
Oh, are you finished?

473
00:29:57,462 --> 00:29:58,379
Hm?

474
00:30:00,215 --> 00:30:01,132
-Then…
-Mm.

475
00:30:01,716 --> 00:30:05,637
"Please let me know if you have received
any new orders from the major."

476
00:30:05,720 --> 00:30:07,388
If you could add that to the end.

477
00:30:07,472 --> 00:30:10,141
It sounds more like a report
than a letter.

478
00:30:10,225 --> 00:30:11,100
Okay.

479
00:30:11,184 --> 00:30:13,478
Now it is my turn
to write your letter, Ms. Luculia.

480
00:30:13,561 --> 00:30:14,395
Oh.

481
00:30:15,396 --> 00:30:17,023
Let's see. My bro…

482
00:30:17,106 --> 00:30:19,734
No. I'll address it to my parents.

483
00:30:19,818 --> 00:30:20,777
Understood.

484
00:30:20,860 --> 00:30:25,031
I, um… I haven't been able
to really thank my mother and father

485
00:30:25,114 --> 00:30:26,825
for everything they've done yet.

486
00:30:27,867 --> 00:30:28,993
Hmm.

487
00:30:29,077 --> 00:30:31,746
It's hard to express exactly what to say

488
00:30:31,830 --> 00:30:33,790
when it's time
to actually write the letter.

489
00:30:33,873 --> 00:30:36,584
Oh, and all the places
we've been to together,

490
00:30:36,668 --> 00:30:38,419
and the places we wanted to go.

491
00:30:38,503 --> 00:30:40,797
There's just so many to list.

492
00:30:42,173 --> 00:30:45,051
"See you soon.
You don't need to worry about me.

493
00:30:45,134 --> 00:30:47,136
Sincerely, Luculia."

494
00:30:52,225 --> 00:30:53,726
Hmm.

495
00:30:53,810 --> 00:30:56,312
Would you mind reading this for me?

496
00:30:57,063 --> 00:30:57,981
Yes, ma'am.

497
00:30:59,732 --> 00:31:01,109
"Dear Father and Mother,

498
00:31:01,192 --> 00:31:05,780
it has been a while since we last spoke,
but I have nothing specific to report.

499
00:31:05,864 --> 00:31:08,366
I worry that I have not expressed
my gratitude

500
00:31:08,449 --> 00:31:09,742
for our previous engagements.

501
00:31:10,326 --> 00:31:13,246
Regarding the places we have been
and desired to go,

502
00:31:13,329 --> 00:31:14,998
I have nothing to report.

503
00:31:15,081 --> 00:31:17,917
I am currently working very diligently.

504
00:31:18,001 --> 00:31:20,420
I am currently healthy and safe.

505
00:31:20,503 --> 00:31:22,005
There have been no issues.

506
00:31:22,088 --> 00:31:23,339
That is all.

507
00:31:23,423 --> 00:31:26,259
Please do not be concerned. Luculia."

508
00:31:26,342 --> 00:31:29,262
And do you really believe
this is a viable letter?

509
00:31:30,930 --> 00:31:35,727
Oh, well, it could be that I was
a little too abstract in expressing it.

510
00:31:35,810 --> 00:31:37,687
That is not the issue here.

511
00:31:37,770 --> 00:31:41,357
Letters are about communicating
a person's true feelings.

512
00:31:41,441 --> 00:31:44,652
An admirable Doll
will be able to find those feelings

513
00:31:44,736 --> 00:31:47,697
that the people want to communicate
from their words.

514
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:49,324
Violet,

515
00:31:49,407 --> 00:31:53,369
your grades are excellent
and your typing is very fast and accurate.

516
00:31:54,162 --> 00:31:56,456
However, what you have written
on her behalf

517
00:31:56,539 --> 00:31:58,333
can hardly be called a letter.

518
00:31:59,250 --> 00:32:01,210
You cannot call this a letter?

519
00:32:01,920 --> 00:32:05,131
-Um, I could try again--
-That is all for today.

520
00:32:06,925 --> 00:32:09,218
You just had an off day today.

521
00:32:10,345 --> 00:32:13,765
Except that this is not the first time
someone has told me that.

522
00:32:13,848 --> 00:32:14,682
I see.

523
00:32:19,520 --> 00:32:22,690
I know.
I'll show you the best view in the city.

524
00:32:22,774 --> 00:32:24,192
What do you say?

525
00:32:28,446 --> 00:32:29,572
It's here.

526
00:32:32,784 --> 00:32:34,160
Be sure to watch your step.

527
00:32:54,430 --> 00:32:56,307
Beautiful, right?

528
00:32:56,391 --> 00:32:59,102
I've always loved this view
since I was a child.

529
00:32:59,185 --> 00:33:01,104
We used to come here.

530
00:33:02,855 --> 00:33:04,190
Violet.

531
00:33:06,192 --> 00:33:07,694
I hope that one day…

532
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:12,740
you'll be able to see
that beautiful view in Leiden.

533
00:33:19,163 --> 00:33:20,707
Well, I'm going this way.

534
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:22,125
See you tomorrow.

535
00:33:23,751 --> 00:33:24,669
Ms. Luculia.

536
00:33:24,752 --> 00:33:25,837
Uh?

537
00:33:27,338 --> 00:33:29,215
You can just call me Luculia, okay?

538
00:33:29,298 --> 00:33:31,009
Go home already.

539
00:33:31,092 --> 00:33:33,720
Come on, don't be like that.
Just one more.

540
00:33:34,721 --> 00:33:38,016
Brother! Were you drinking again?

541
00:33:38,099 --> 00:33:40,059
What? No, I wasn't.

542
00:33:40,143 --> 00:33:41,144
I said go home.

543
00:33:41,227 --> 00:33:43,938
I haven't had a drink
because he won't let…

544
00:33:44,022 --> 00:33:45,148
Oh!

545
00:33:45,231 --> 00:33:46,774
Spencer! Are you okay?

546
00:33:49,110 --> 00:33:50,069
Leave.

547
00:33:57,660 --> 00:33:59,203
Luculia.

548
00:34:00,038 --> 00:34:01,497
It's okay. Thanks.

549
00:34:02,874 --> 00:34:03,958
Violet…

550
00:34:04,042 --> 00:34:04,876
-Hmp!
-Hmp!

551
00:34:04,959 --> 00:34:06,127
…while I'm happy for the letter,

552
00:34:06,210 --> 00:34:08,671
it actually feels
a little more like a report.

553
00:34:09,672 --> 00:34:15,011
My instructor also said that what I wrote
could not be called a letter.

554
00:34:16,721 --> 00:34:17,555
So will I…

555
00:34:18,264 --> 00:34:20,892
be able to become an admirable Doll?

556
00:34:24,562 --> 00:34:25,646
Bluebell Junoa.

557
00:34:26,230 --> 00:34:28,149
-Yes.
-Iberis Konoue.

558
00:34:28,232 --> 00:34:29,817
Yes.

559
00:34:29,901 --> 00:34:31,611
Luculia Marlborough.

560
00:34:33,321 --> 00:34:34,655
Luculia Marlborough?

561
00:34:34,739 --> 00:34:35,782
Oh!

562
00:34:35,865 --> 00:34:36,991
Here!

563
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:40,244
Congratulations to the nine of you
for graduating our program.

564
00:34:40,328 --> 00:34:43,873
I hope that all of you
become admirable Dolls.

565
00:34:43,956 --> 00:34:46,709
We did it!
Where are you going to work?

566
00:34:46,793 --> 00:34:48,669
I'm going to work in my hometown.

567
00:34:48,753 --> 00:34:50,963
I think I'll find something in Leiden.

568
00:34:51,047 --> 00:34:52,465
What about you, Luculia?

569
00:34:52,548 --> 00:34:53,758
Huh?

570
00:34:53,841 --> 00:34:55,093
Well, I…

571
00:34:55,176 --> 00:34:57,637
I actually haven't decided
anything as of yet.

572
00:34:57,720 --> 00:35:00,181
What?
But you were the top of our class.

573
00:35:00,973 --> 00:35:04,018
I see. It's unfortunate.

574
00:35:04,102 --> 00:35:05,394
I am sorry to disappoint you.

575
00:35:06,646 --> 00:35:07,855
Oh, it's all right.

576
00:35:08,356 --> 00:35:11,400
Not graduating doesn't really mean
you can't become a Doll.

577
00:35:12,026 --> 00:35:12,902
Then…

578
00:35:13,528 --> 00:35:15,905
what was the purpose
for going to that school?

579
00:35:18,324 --> 00:35:21,410
While it is true
that graduating is not everything,

580
00:35:22,120 --> 00:35:24,413
if I am unable to understand the feelings

581
00:35:24,497 --> 00:35:26,624
they wish to communicate from their words,

582
00:35:27,959 --> 00:35:30,461
then there is no point in being a Doll.

583
00:35:41,764 --> 00:35:43,224
I knew you would come here.

584
00:35:44,684 --> 00:35:46,060
Luculia.

585
00:35:46,144 --> 00:35:49,564
Why are you here? The program is over now.

586
00:35:50,815 --> 00:35:53,985
Because I knew you'd be here
and I wanted to talk to you.

587
00:35:55,486 --> 00:35:56,821
Tell me, Violet…

588
00:35:57,989 --> 00:35:59,240
Who is the major?

589
00:36:00,825 --> 00:36:03,327
When you write your letters,
you always end it with

590
00:36:03,411 --> 00:36:05,705
"Has the major sent me any letters yet?"

591
00:36:05,788 --> 00:36:07,331
And so I was thinking,

592
00:36:07,415 --> 00:36:10,835
isn't he the one that you really want
to send a letter to?

593
00:36:10,918 --> 00:36:14,338
I know.
Why don't we write a letter to him today?

594
00:36:14,422 --> 00:36:16,924
You know, not like your usual reports,

595
00:36:17,008 --> 00:36:19,886
but a letter that actually shows
what your feelings are.

596
00:36:22,180 --> 00:36:24,265
I won't leave until we're done.

597
00:36:30,229 --> 00:36:31,189
Major…

598
00:36:36,277 --> 00:36:37,361
I'm sorry.

599
00:36:38,321 --> 00:36:41,240
You see, the reality is that
I have no idea

600
00:36:41,949 --> 00:36:43,993
what it is that I want to say to him.

601
00:36:46,078 --> 00:36:49,749
Because I don't even understand
the meaning of the words he gave me.

602
00:36:50,333 --> 00:36:51,834
I am confused.

603
00:36:54,420 --> 00:36:58,049
Violet, why did you want
to become a Doll?

604
00:37:01,719 --> 00:37:05,014
Because I…
I want to know what "I love you" means.

605
00:37:05,097 --> 00:37:06,057
Oh.

606
00:37:06,641 --> 00:37:09,018
What does it mean? I see.

607
00:37:11,062 --> 00:37:13,606
It's hard to communicate
your feelings, isn't it?

608
00:37:16,108 --> 00:37:19,862
The truth is
that my parents have passed away.

609
00:37:21,405 --> 00:37:23,032
So all I have left

610
00:37:23,115 --> 00:37:24,575
is my brother Spencer.

611
00:37:25,117 --> 00:37:30,122
To be honest, sometimes I don't even know
what I'm supposed to say to him.

612
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:33,167
When the war began,

613
00:37:33,793 --> 00:37:36,254
my brother went off to fight as a soldier.

614
00:37:36,337 --> 00:37:37,755
But the truth is,

615
00:37:37,838 --> 00:37:40,967
there wasn't much fighting
on the Western Front.

616
00:37:41,050 --> 00:37:42,343
That's where he was deployed.

617
00:37:43,511 --> 00:37:46,180
The fighting always seemed
to be happening somewhere else.

618
00:37:46,847 --> 00:37:49,016
The war didn't seem real to us.

619
00:37:50,017 --> 00:37:51,519
It was just the stories.

620
00:37:52,561 --> 00:37:53,604
But…

621
00:37:54,522 --> 00:37:58,567
one day, when my parents
went to Herne for business…

622
00:37:58,651 --> 00:38:01,362
the Western Front was broken.

623
00:38:02,780 --> 00:38:07,535
They looked all over for my parents
but couldn't find any trace of them.

624
00:38:10,913 --> 00:38:12,373
And then the war ended.

625
00:38:14,458 --> 00:38:16,627
-My brother came home alive.
-Come on, just one drink, okay?

626
00:38:16,711 --> 00:38:17,753
Give it a rest, would ya?

627
00:38:17,837 --> 00:38:21,382
I wanted to be happy
that at least he was alive.

628
00:38:21,465 --> 00:38:22,300
What the hell?

629
00:38:22,383 --> 00:38:23,801
-But my brother was angry…
-Shut up!

630
00:38:23,884 --> 00:38:25,928
…that he wasn't able to protect Herne.

631
00:38:26,762 --> 00:38:29,473
Angry that he wasn't there
for our parents.

632
00:38:30,266 --> 00:38:32,059
He blames himself for their deaths.

633
00:38:36,022 --> 00:38:38,566
Don't show your face around here again.

634
00:38:44,864 --> 00:38:45,948
I was just…

635
00:38:46,699 --> 00:38:48,367
You see, I was just…

636
00:38:49,535 --> 00:38:51,954
I was just happy that he was alive.

637
00:38:58,294 --> 00:38:59,545
I only wanted to…

638
00:39:00,338 --> 00:39:01,589
to say "thank you."

639
00:39:05,051 --> 00:39:05,885
But…

640
00:39:07,178 --> 00:39:08,554
I can't.

641
00:39:12,808 --> 00:39:13,642
Luculia.

642
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:15,728
Let's write a letter.

643
00:39:18,064 --> 00:39:20,816
Let's put all of your feelings
into that letter.

644
00:39:20,900 --> 00:39:22,193
Say what you want.

645
00:39:25,321 --> 00:39:29,116
Yeah, but whenever I think about
telling him how I feel,

646
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:30,618
nothing comes out.

647
00:39:31,494 --> 00:39:34,163
I've tried so many times
in the past.

648
00:39:35,373 --> 00:39:36,749
But it's no use.

649
00:39:37,750 --> 00:39:39,627
I'm sure I never will.

650
00:39:40,294 --> 00:39:42,380
Thank you, Violet.

651
00:39:42,463 --> 00:39:44,799
We'll write your letter to the major
another time.

652
00:39:52,306 --> 00:39:54,058
An admirable Doll can…

653
00:39:54,934 --> 00:39:56,310
find the true feelings

654
00:39:57,019 --> 00:40:00,314
a client wants to communicate
from their words.

655
00:40:10,908 --> 00:40:12,076
Spencer!

656
00:40:13,828 --> 00:40:15,037
Spencer, wait!

657
00:40:15,704 --> 00:40:16,914
Come on.

658
00:40:17,540 --> 00:40:18,916
Hm.

659
00:40:20,668 --> 00:40:21,836
Thanks.

660
00:40:24,088 --> 00:40:25,548
Hurry up. This way.

661
00:40:28,592 --> 00:40:31,220
Oh, wow! Pretty!

662
00:40:32,346 --> 00:40:33,597
Whoa!

663
00:40:55,911 --> 00:40:57,329
Wait. You're…

664
00:40:57,413 --> 00:40:59,331
You're Luculia's friend.

665
00:41:01,542 --> 00:41:04,003
-What's this?
-A mission.

666
00:41:04,086 --> 00:41:05,588
No, an assignment.

667
00:41:07,465 --> 00:41:09,091
No, it's a letter.

668
00:41:09,175 --> 00:41:11,469
It is from Luculia to you.

669
00:41:13,137 --> 00:41:14,597
From Luculia?

670
00:41:27,651 --> 00:41:30,738
"To my brother. I'm happy.

671
00:41:30,821 --> 00:41:32,239
I'm happy that…

672
00:41:32,865 --> 00:41:34,283
that you are alive."

673
00:41:37,077 --> 00:41:38,746
"Thank you."

674
00:41:38,829 --> 00:41:40,414
LUCULIA MARLBOROUGH

675
00:42:01,477 --> 00:42:02,603
Violet! I was…

676
00:42:04,021 --> 00:42:05,105
-Luculia.
-Huh?

677
00:42:05,189 --> 00:42:06,607
Is something wrong?

678
00:42:11,070 --> 00:42:13,239
Good morning to you, Violet.

679
00:42:13,822 --> 00:42:16,617
Instructor. Is school not finished?

680
00:42:17,243 --> 00:42:19,828
I'm sorry, I'm the one who asked her here.

681
00:42:20,829 --> 00:42:23,749
Luculia has decided
to show me this letter.

682
00:42:23,832 --> 00:42:27,628
The letter you wrote
on behalf of Luculia for her brother.

683
00:42:28,337 --> 00:42:32,633
You see, the feelings
I've been wanting to tell my brother.

684
00:42:33,300 --> 00:42:34,426
Violet,

685
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:37,054
you were able to tell him for me.

686
00:42:40,140 --> 00:42:42,101
An admirable Doll

687
00:42:42,184 --> 00:42:45,854
must find the true feelings
the client wishes to communicate

688
00:42:45,938 --> 00:42:47,690
from the words they tell you.

689
00:42:48,691 --> 00:42:52,486
You were able to take that step.

690
00:42:53,779 --> 00:42:54,863
Violet.

691
00:42:57,825 --> 00:43:00,786
I truly hope you become an admirable Doll.

692
00:43:02,538 --> 00:43:05,916
Yesterday's play was so good, wasn't it?

693
00:43:06,625 --> 00:43:09,086
You should have come with us, Violet.

694
00:43:09,169 --> 00:43:11,505
If you mean the Red Demon,
I am reading the play now.

695
00:43:12,590 --> 00:43:14,800
Ah, I'm so jealous.

696
00:43:14,883 --> 00:43:18,137
I would have loved to scribe
for Oscar Webster.

697
00:43:18,220 --> 00:43:20,889
It means you get to read
his new work first, doesn't it?

698
00:43:20,973 --> 00:43:23,267
It'll be his first new work in a while.

699
00:43:23,350 --> 00:43:25,436
I can't wait to see how it turns out.

700
00:43:28,147 --> 00:43:30,441
"Ah, I must suffer
the consequences

701
00:43:30,524 --> 00:43:32,318
of the sins I have committed.

702
00:43:32,401 --> 00:43:34,236
For the rest of my life."

703
00:43:37,156 --> 00:43:40,075
GENETRIX
ROSWELL REGION

704
00:43:59,428 --> 00:44:00,554
Who is it?

705
00:44:00,638 --> 00:44:02,765
It's the Auto Memories Doll service.

706
00:44:03,682 --> 00:44:05,517
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

707
00:44:06,560 --> 00:44:08,187
It is a pleasure to meet you.

708
00:44:09,355 --> 00:44:12,274
If it is your wish,
I will travel anywhere to meet you.

709
00:44:12,858 --> 00:44:15,027
Auto Memories Doll at your service.

710
00:44:15,861 --> 00:44:17,404
Violet Evergarden.

711
00:44:19,031 --> 00:44:20,532
What a surprise.

712
00:44:20,616 --> 00:44:23,035
I wasn't expecting such a child.

713
00:44:23,827 --> 00:44:25,829
If I am not to your satisfaction,

714
00:44:25,913 --> 00:44:28,707
I can arrange for another Doll
to take my place.

715
00:44:28,791 --> 00:44:31,251
No, as long as you can type.

716
00:44:32,294 --> 00:44:34,630
My health hasn't been the best lately.

717
00:44:36,215 --> 00:44:38,133
I am terribly sorry,

718
00:44:38,217 --> 00:44:42,096
but I will ask you to refrain from alcohol
while we work together.

719
00:44:44,431 --> 00:44:46,308
I can't write unless I drink!

720
00:44:46,892 --> 00:44:48,560
I will be the one writing.

721
00:44:48,644 --> 00:44:51,188
Then let's start work tomorrow.

722
00:44:54,566 --> 00:44:56,402
Why must you be so difficult?

723
00:45:03,659 --> 00:45:04,660
Excuse me.

724
00:45:05,536 --> 00:45:08,414
I have cleaned the area
for a better writing environment.

725
00:45:08,997 --> 00:45:10,999
I have brought my own typewriter.

726
00:45:11,625 --> 00:45:13,419
Do you have typing paper?

727
00:45:13,502 --> 00:45:16,755
I don't, sorry.
They sell it at the store by the port.

728
00:45:16,839 --> 00:45:17,965
Go buy some.

729
00:45:18,632 --> 00:45:22,428
And dinner, too, while you're at it.
I want carbonara.

730
00:45:23,262 --> 00:45:24,763
I'm sorry, sir.

731
00:45:24,847 --> 00:45:26,974
I'm only here to be a scribe, not a maid.

732
00:45:27,599 --> 00:45:28,434
Hm?

733
00:45:30,686 --> 00:45:32,438
Why must he be so difficult?

734
00:45:35,065 --> 00:45:37,693
I've got all the ingredients
you need right here.

735
00:45:37,776 --> 00:45:39,194
Thank you very much.

736
00:45:40,821 --> 00:45:43,824
What's the matter?
Is there a problem with it?

737
00:45:43,907 --> 00:45:47,953
No, I was just wondering
how I'm supposed to cook this.

738
00:45:48,036 --> 00:45:51,874
Hm? Well, you crack the egg
and then you separate the yolk.

739
00:45:51,957 --> 00:45:52,958
The yolk?

740
00:46:01,925 --> 00:46:03,343
Um, what are you doing?

741
00:46:04,261 --> 00:46:06,305
I am trying my hand at cooking.

742
00:46:16,565 --> 00:46:20,694
Well, you know, it's actually
pretty good for your first try.

743
00:46:20,778 --> 00:46:24,990
-Are you not going to have any?
-No. I will have some later.

744
00:46:25,073 --> 00:46:26,200
I see.

745
00:46:35,042 --> 00:46:36,543
Next is Olive's line.

746
00:46:37,920 --> 00:46:39,838
"We must cross this valley of fire

747
00:46:40,631 --> 00:46:43,133
in order to get the sword
to slay the monster."

748
00:46:43,759 --> 00:46:46,970
Stage direction. "Enter a water spirit."

749
00:46:47,054 --> 00:46:48,722
The spirit's line.

750
00:46:48,806 --> 00:46:51,517
"I will put out this fire for you.

751
00:46:51,600 --> 00:46:54,019
Then you will be able
to cross this valley."

752
00:46:55,020 --> 00:46:57,815
So, they'll be able to cross it?
Thank goodness.

753
00:46:57,898 --> 00:47:02,069
Stage direction.
"The burning fire is extinguished."

754
00:47:02,152 --> 00:47:03,904
How will it be extinguished?

755
00:47:04,655 --> 00:47:07,574
If they pull in the red cloth
that was waving around the stage,

756
00:47:07,658 --> 00:47:09,868
it will look like it's been put out.

757
00:47:10,619 --> 00:47:13,205
I see. I understand.

758
00:47:14,248 --> 00:47:16,208
So, what are you thinking?

759
00:47:16,291 --> 00:47:17,584
Is it good?

760
00:47:19,461 --> 00:47:20,921
How do I put this?

761
00:47:21,004 --> 00:47:22,631
Just be honest with me.

762
00:47:22,714 --> 00:47:25,217
Even though it didn't really happen,

763
00:47:25,801 --> 00:47:28,011
it's as if I'm experiencing it.

764
00:47:28,095 --> 00:47:29,012
Ah.

765
00:47:29,596 --> 00:47:32,766
I find myself feeling
like this girl, Olive.

766
00:47:32,850 --> 00:47:35,519
Feeling happy, and feeling sad.

767
00:47:35,602 --> 00:47:38,021
I feel uncertain about it.

768
00:47:38,105 --> 00:47:39,606
Why is that?

769
00:47:39,690 --> 00:47:40,899
Huh.

770
00:47:41,525 --> 00:47:46,029
Because you're feeling what Olive is.

771
00:47:46,113 --> 00:47:48,532
You're beginning to identify with her.

772
00:47:49,408 --> 00:47:51,410
You feel empathy with Olive.

773
00:47:54,037 --> 00:47:56,957
I'm relieved that you feel that way.

774
00:47:57,875 --> 00:48:01,461
This is my first time writing a play
that's meant for children.

775
00:48:02,921 --> 00:48:06,341
After this, Olive will be able
to cross the valley of fire,

776
00:48:06,425 --> 00:48:09,469
find the sword,
and slay the monster, won't she?

777
00:48:10,220 --> 00:48:11,346
That's right.

778
00:48:11,430 --> 00:48:16,184
Although, in the process, she loses
her power to commune with the spirits.

779
00:48:16,268 --> 00:48:17,644
Oh, no.

780
00:48:17,728 --> 00:48:20,314
But in that case,
how is she going to return home?

781
00:48:20,397 --> 00:48:22,566
She has already lost her boat.

782
00:48:22,649 --> 00:48:23,734
Hmm.

783
00:48:24,526 --> 00:48:26,778
I haven't come up with that part yet.

784
00:48:26,862 --> 00:48:27,905
You have to.

785
00:48:29,406 --> 00:48:30,240
Or she…

786
00:48:30,949 --> 00:48:33,201
can't return to her waiting father.

787
00:48:36,747 --> 00:48:37,956
Do you have an idea?

788
00:48:44,254 --> 00:48:46,048
The weather is nice today.

789
00:48:46,131 --> 00:48:48,800
No, it's too good.

790
00:48:50,385 --> 00:48:52,054
-Sir.
-Huh.

791
00:48:52,638 --> 00:48:53,931
Huh?

792
00:48:54,681 --> 00:48:55,933
What is this?

793
00:48:56,016 --> 00:48:59,186
Oh, it's just a parasol.

794
00:48:59,937 --> 00:49:00,854
Why do you ask?

795
00:49:01,480 --> 00:49:04,399
Because I think it's beautiful.

796
00:49:09,738 --> 00:49:10,697
Let me…

797
00:49:11,281 --> 00:49:12,658
take a little break.

798
00:49:28,674 --> 00:49:29,591
One day…

799
00:49:30,258 --> 00:49:32,219
I promise to show you one day.

800
00:49:33,762 --> 00:49:35,222
Stop it!

801
00:49:39,017 --> 00:49:40,185
Please, stop it.

802
00:49:40,268 --> 00:49:42,104
I apologize, sir.

803
00:49:42,187 --> 00:49:44,272
-I shouldn't have--
-That's enough!

804
00:49:45,482 --> 00:49:46,817
That's enough.

805
00:49:47,776 --> 00:49:48,735
Go home.

806
00:49:51,822 --> 00:49:54,241
Then the play will not be completed.

807
00:49:54,324 --> 00:49:57,244
Olive's story will never be completed.

808
00:49:58,203 --> 00:49:59,246
Sir, please wait!

809
00:49:59,329 --> 00:50:02,416
Is there something
you're hiding inside your heart?

810
00:50:04,710 --> 00:50:09,006
You see, I… I'm unable
to sense those feelings.

811
00:50:10,007 --> 00:50:12,592
I am… very sorry.

812
00:50:15,637 --> 00:50:18,724
I… I can't write anything anymore.

813
00:50:19,307 --> 00:50:21,560
But I can't let it end like this.

814
00:50:22,185 --> 00:50:24,021
So, that's why

815
00:50:24,604 --> 00:50:28,358
I thought I would finish the story.
The one I told Olivia.

816
00:50:29,484 --> 00:50:30,485
Olivia?

817
00:50:31,111 --> 00:50:32,279
Yes.

818
00:50:33,363 --> 00:50:34,322
My daughter.

819
00:50:36,283 --> 00:50:40,287
After I lost my wife to illness,
I moved here with my daughter.

820
00:50:41,496 --> 00:50:43,540
This used to be our summer home.

821
00:50:46,084 --> 00:50:48,420
I think she was sad not having a mother.

822
00:50:48,503 --> 00:50:49,713
But…

823
00:50:50,464 --> 00:50:52,591
she never actually showed it.

824
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:59,473
Rather, she always helped me
so I could focus on my work.

825
00:51:01,475 --> 00:51:05,896
My daughter's favorite things
were silly frilled parasol

826
00:51:06,688 --> 00:51:07,606
and water birds.

827
00:51:09,775 --> 00:51:11,193
Wow!

828
00:51:11,902 --> 00:51:13,070
I'm so jealous.

829
00:51:13,653 --> 00:51:16,031
I want to try crossing this lake, too.

830
00:51:16,531 --> 00:51:19,409
Do you think I could walk on those leaves?

831
00:51:20,160 --> 00:51:21,411
Hm.

832
00:51:21,495 --> 00:51:24,915
Maybe if you let the wind carry you
with your parasol.

833
00:51:30,212 --> 00:51:31,338
Olivia!

834
00:51:32,506 --> 00:51:33,423
I'm okay.

835
00:51:35,300 --> 00:51:37,636
I'm going to walk across this lake.

836
00:51:38,678 --> 00:51:40,514
I promise to show you one day.

837
00:51:41,681 --> 00:51:42,808
Okay, Daddy?

838
00:51:46,228 --> 00:51:47,479
And then…

839
00:51:50,190 --> 00:51:52,484
after arguing with the doctors,

840
00:51:53,151 --> 00:51:58,323
I decided to bring her back here
to spend what time she had left.

841
00:51:59,449 --> 00:52:01,701
It was good to see her smile again.

842
00:52:02,744 --> 00:52:05,705
Our days were quiet and warm.

843
00:52:06,289 --> 00:52:07,124
But…

844
00:52:09,251 --> 00:52:10,919
my only hope…

845
00:52:11,753 --> 00:52:15,674
Why does God take what is most precious?

846
00:52:17,717 --> 00:52:21,179
Parting with someone
who is important to you…

847
00:52:21,763 --> 00:52:24,432
Never being able to see them again…

848
00:52:25,934 --> 00:52:27,477
I never knew…

849
00:52:29,312 --> 00:52:32,816
that it was so sad and painful.

850
00:52:45,120 --> 00:52:48,123
I'm sorry for earlier today.

851
00:52:48,206 --> 00:52:51,585
No, you are the one who's truly in pain.

852
00:52:51,668 --> 00:52:54,880
I apologize for being the one
to lose composure.

853
00:52:55,589 --> 00:52:56,631
I will finish it.

854
00:52:58,216 --> 00:52:59,926
I'll finish Olive's story.

855
00:53:00,510 --> 00:53:03,972
The girl will reach her home
and be with her father.

856
00:53:04,055 --> 00:53:08,685
No matter how difficult the adventure,
she… will have a happy ending.

857
00:53:09,811 --> 00:53:13,398
Both Olive and the audience will be happy.

858
00:53:14,024 --> 00:53:14,900
I will do it.

859
00:53:18,695 --> 00:53:20,864
The monster falls.

860
00:53:20,947 --> 00:53:21,907
Olive.

861
00:53:21,990 --> 00:53:24,826
"We finally slayed the monster."

862
00:53:24,910 --> 00:53:26,119
Water spirit.

863
00:53:26,203 --> 00:53:27,996
"You did very well."

864
00:53:28,079 --> 00:53:29,497
Wind spirit says,

865
00:53:29,581 --> 00:53:31,958
"We must return to the spirit realm."

866
00:53:32,042 --> 00:53:33,835
The Fire spirit says,

867
00:53:33,919 --> 00:53:35,462
"This is goodbye."

868
00:53:35,545 --> 00:53:37,088
Olive stands there.

869
00:53:37,172 --> 00:53:39,007
Completely unable to move.

870
00:53:40,008 --> 00:53:44,512
Now, then, how do we go about
getting Olive home from here?

871
00:53:45,305 --> 00:53:48,308
Since her boat sank, can she take a plane?

872
00:53:48,892 --> 00:53:49,809
Hm.

873
00:53:50,477 --> 00:53:52,646
Maybe something a little more imaginative.

874
00:53:54,105 --> 00:53:56,191
She could fly home if she were a bird.

875
00:53:58,109 --> 00:54:00,028
What about the parasol?

876
00:54:00,111 --> 00:54:01,571
You cannot fly with a parasol.

877
00:54:01,655 --> 00:54:02,739
But she can!

878
00:54:02,822 --> 00:54:06,117
The Wind Spirit appears before her
one last time and says,

879
00:54:06,201 --> 00:54:08,787
"Olive, open your parasol."

880
00:54:09,955 --> 00:54:13,291
Will you please
try opening the parasol for me?

881
00:54:15,377 --> 00:54:17,545
"That parasol is your wings.

882
00:54:17,629 --> 00:54:20,048
You'll be carried away
if you fly too high.

883
00:54:20,131 --> 00:54:22,384
So, step on the ocean's waves,

884
00:54:22,467 --> 00:54:26,554
the river's rocks,
and the lake's fallen leaves."

885
00:54:26,638 --> 00:54:28,056
That's a great idea.

886
00:54:28,139 --> 00:54:32,769
Okay, after returning home,
Olive reunites with her father.

887
00:54:32,852 --> 00:54:34,104
And then,

888
00:54:34,187 --> 00:54:38,066
the first thing she says when they're
reunited after crossing the ocean…

889
00:54:38,149 --> 00:54:39,484
What should it be?

890
00:54:40,068 --> 00:54:41,444
"I'm home."

891
00:54:41,528 --> 00:54:43,530
No, "Father?"

892
00:54:43,613 --> 00:54:45,782
Sir, do you have writer's block again?

893
00:54:45,865 --> 00:54:46,950
Hm.

894
00:54:47,701 --> 00:54:50,787
Could you walk towards me from over there?

895
00:54:50,870 --> 00:54:52,414
I'd like to visualize it.

896
00:54:53,039 --> 00:54:54,958
I only need to walk?

897
00:54:55,041 --> 00:54:58,128
Yes. Across the fallen leaves
on the lake if you can.

898
00:54:58,962 --> 00:54:59,963
Copy that.

899
00:55:01,589 --> 00:55:02,799
Huh?

900
00:55:02,882 --> 00:55:05,176
No, that last bit was just…

901
00:55:24,279 --> 00:55:25,697
I'm so jealous.

902
00:55:27,198 --> 00:55:29,576
I want to try crossing this lake, too.

903
00:55:31,077 --> 00:55:33,330
Do you think I could walk on those leaves?

904
00:55:36,958 --> 00:55:38,209
One day…

905
00:55:38,960 --> 00:55:40,795
I promise to show you one day.

906
00:55:41,921 --> 00:55:43,089
Okay, Daddy?

907
00:55:47,761 --> 00:55:52,390
How I wish I could hear you
call me thata thousand times more.

908
00:55:55,101 --> 00:55:56,353
I wish…

909
00:55:56,436 --> 00:55:59,022
you didn't have to die.

910
00:55:59,731 --> 00:56:02,859
If only you could have lived, grown up…

911
00:56:08,698 --> 00:56:11,368
How I wished that for you.

912
00:56:31,638 --> 00:56:33,306
Were you able to see?

913
00:56:36,351 --> 00:56:38,603
I almost made it the entire way.

914
00:56:41,356 --> 00:56:42,440
Sir?

915
00:56:43,817 --> 00:56:44,859
What's the matter?

916
00:56:45,527 --> 00:56:47,153
Are you feeling ill?

917
00:56:50,740 --> 00:56:53,827
Are you sure I can have this parasol?

918
00:56:54,828 --> 00:56:55,662
Yes.

919
00:56:56,538 --> 00:56:59,165
I thought that I could fly
a little further.

920
00:56:59,249 --> 00:57:00,750
You went far enough.

921
00:57:01,418 --> 00:57:04,754
You were able to fulfill
my Olivia's wish for "one day".

922
00:57:07,257 --> 00:57:09,801
Her wish for one day?

923
00:57:12,971 --> 00:57:13,930
Well, then.

924
00:57:14,597 --> 00:57:17,475
Thank you for using
our Auto Memories Doll service.

925
00:57:18,435 --> 00:57:20,478
It was a pleasure working with you.

926
00:57:21,062 --> 00:57:22,730
You have my gratitude.

927
00:57:23,940 --> 00:57:26,609
Violet Evergarden.

928
00:57:35,535 --> 00:57:38,413
You see, your soul is on fire.

929
00:57:38,496 --> 00:57:40,290
You're burning up right now

930
00:57:40,373 --> 00:57:42,459
because of the things you did.

931
00:57:44,127 --> 00:57:46,212
-I'm not--
-Yes, you are.

932
00:57:46,921 --> 00:57:49,257
You'll understand what I mean someday.

933
00:57:50,341 --> 00:57:54,596
And then you'll realize for the first time
that you have many burns.

934
00:58:02,979 --> 00:58:03,813
Major.

935
00:58:04,564 --> 00:58:05,440
Just live.

936
00:58:06,107 --> 00:58:07,275
Am I allowed to?

937
00:58:08,193 --> 00:58:09,986
You have to be free.

938
00:58:10,778 --> 00:58:12,947
Am I really allowed to live…

939
00:58:13,948 --> 00:58:16,034
after killing so many?

940
00:58:17,285 --> 00:58:20,455
Have I not taken away
someone's "one day" before?

941
00:58:23,917 --> 00:58:27,587
And did those people
not have people they loved as well?

942
00:58:28,296 --> 00:58:29,714
I'm not burning.

943
00:58:30,298 --> 00:58:31,216
I am burning!

944
00:58:31,299 --> 00:58:32,717
I am not burning.

945
00:58:32,800 --> 00:58:34,052
I am burning!

946
00:58:34,677 --> 00:58:38,681
I feel the fire spreading
from all the things I've done.

947
00:58:38,765 --> 00:58:39,933
I'm on fire.

948
00:58:52,820 --> 00:58:54,072
Oh?

949
00:58:54,822 --> 00:58:57,492
Violet, it's nice to see you.

950
00:58:57,575 --> 00:58:58,785
Madam.

951
00:58:59,494 --> 00:59:02,497
Please forgive me for my past actions.

952
00:59:03,081 --> 00:59:07,585
I sincerely apologize.
It was never my intention to offend you.

953
00:59:08,461 --> 00:59:13,258
Oh, Violet, dear. Now, now,
you don't have to apologize for anything.

954
00:59:16,761 --> 00:59:19,973
I'm so thankful
to see how far you've come.

955
00:59:20,056 --> 00:59:22,892
I am sure Gilbert can rest in peace, too.

956
00:59:27,605 --> 00:59:28,815
Rest in peace?

957
00:59:31,401 --> 00:59:33,903
You said he was alive, didn't you?

958
00:59:33,987 --> 00:59:36,072
The major is safe, isn't he?

959
00:59:37,532 --> 00:59:38,616
Well, uh…

960
00:59:39,117 --> 00:59:41,578
He's alive. He just has to be!

961
00:59:46,249 --> 00:59:47,417
I'm sorry.

962
00:59:48,251 --> 00:59:51,004
I just couldn't bring myself to tell you.

963
00:59:52,130 --> 00:59:54,924
After the Final Battle of Intense,

964
00:59:55,008 --> 00:59:58,344
you were found alone on the ground
under a church.

965
00:59:59,554 --> 01:00:03,808
Most likely, he pushed you away
right before it was bombarded.

966
01:00:05,310 --> 01:00:09,814
While we didn't find his body,
we did find his ID tag under the debris.

967
01:00:10,773 --> 01:00:13,401
So, he was deemed missing in action.

968
01:00:13,484 --> 01:00:15,194
So, we don't know for sure.

969
01:00:15,278 --> 01:00:19,824
-But given the situation…
-I'm sure the major is alive.

970
01:00:19,907 --> 01:00:21,326
Violet, listen, I…

971
01:00:21,409 --> 01:00:22,619
He's alive!

972
01:00:23,536 --> 01:00:26,748
Violet, please understand,
he's already…

973
01:00:26,831 --> 01:00:29,667
I won't. I don't understand.

974
01:00:30,918 --> 01:00:33,379
How could I be the only one to survive?

975
01:00:34,422 --> 01:00:36,299
The major was there with me.

976
01:00:36,883 --> 01:00:38,134
And he…

977
01:00:38,968 --> 01:00:42,639
All right. Now, look, I know it's hard.
You have to accept it.

978
01:00:43,723 --> 01:00:44,974
Violet, wait!

979
01:01:01,324 --> 01:01:02,450
What's your name?

980
01:01:06,788 --> 01:01:08,039
I see.

981
01:01:08,956 --> 01:01:11,876
Would it be okay
if I were to give you a name then?

982
01:01:13,461 --> 01:01:14,379
Huh?

983
01:01:21,344 --> 01:01:22,303
Oh.

984
01:01:30,186 --> 01:01:31,479
Violet.

985
01:01:32,772 --> 01:01:34,107
Your name's Violet.

986
01:01:34,649 --> 01:01:37,360
I have a feeling you'll grow into it
when you're older.

987
01:01:38,945 --> 01:01:41,531
You'll become a person
fitting of that name

988
01:01:42,240 --> 01:01:43,533
and not just a tool.

989
01:01:59,424 --> 01:02:00,258
Hello?

990
01:02:01,259 --> 01:02:02,677
It's you.

991
01:02:04,262 --> 01:02:05,513
I was wondering…

992
01:02:06,180 --> 01:02:08,683
is the major at home right now?

993
01:02:11,352 --> 01:02:12,979
So then, the major has…

994
01:02:13,688 --> 01:02:15,690
He isn't home now, right?

995
01:02:18,234 --> 01:02:19,610
The major is…

996
01:02:36,627 --> 01:02:40,173
Gilbert Bougainvillea.

997
01:02:41,382 --> 01:02:44,469
That's… the major's name.

998
01:03:13,748 --> 01:03:14,957
Major.

999
01:03:20,421 --> 01:03:21,547
What's the matter?

1000
01:03:27,887 --> 01:03:29,180
Hello, Violet.

1001
01:03:33,684 --> 01:03:34,560
Major?

1002
01:03:35,978 --> 01:03:36,813
Major!

1003
01:03:39,023 --> 01:03:40,858
I know that you're alive.

1004
01:03:42,485 --> 01:03:43,444
That outfit.

1005
01:03:45,154 --> 01:03:46,489
It's my job.

1006
01:03:46,572 --> 01:03:49,450
I am currently working
as an Auto Memory Doll.

1007
01:03:50,910 --> 01:03:52,829
-You are?
-Yes.

1008
01:03:53,538 --> 01:03:55,164
I write letters for people.

1009
01:03:58,167 --> 01:03:59,502
Letters, you say?

1010
01:04:01,337 --> 01:04:04,632
With the same hands
that took all those lives?

1011
01:04:12,640 --> 01:04:13,516
Major?

1012
01:04:13,599 --> 01:04:16,561
You're writing letters
meant to connect people together?

1013
01:04:27,947 --> 01:04:28,948
Major?

1014
01:05:53,324 --> 01:05:54,325
Major.

1015
01:05:55,117 --> 01:05:55,952
Major!

1016
01:05:57,078 --> 01:05:59,205
What should I do?

1017
01:06:01,499 --> 01:06:02,541
Please tell me.

1018
01:06:03,918 --> 01:06:05,044
Oh, please.

1019
01:06:06,545 --> 01:06:08,089
Give me an order.

1020
01:06:18,224 --> 01:06:19,809
A letter for you.

1021
01:06:19,892 --> 01:06:21,978
Violet Evergarden.

1022
01:06:32,113 --> 01:06:33,781
This one's addressed to you.

1023
01:06:37,785 --> 01:06:40,371
Erica and Iris asked me to deliver it.

1024
01:06:43,040 --> 01:06:45,459
Very well, I've done my part now.

1025
01:06:49,755 --> 01:06:50,673
It's late.

1026
01:06:50,756 --> 01:06:52,174
You're still delivering?

1027
01:06:53,634 --> 01:06:54,677
Yes.

1028
01:06:54,760 --> 01:06:57,263
Well, I'm heading down
Craft Street.

1029
01:06:57,346 --> 01:07:00,766
Is there any way I could get you
to cover the other route?

1030
01:07:02,435 --> 01:07:03,811
Mm-hm.

1031
01:07:04,937 --> 01:07:06,939
Yes, each one of these letters…

1032
01:07:07,773 --> 01:07:10,317
is someone's precious memory after all.

1033
01:07:11,610 --> 01:07:14,321
And every letter deserves to be delivered.

1034
01:07:24,498 --> 01:07:26,167
It's a letter!

1035
01:07:26,250 --> 01:07:28,085
Mom! It's from Dad!

1036
01:07:43,309 --> 01:07:45,102
Have you finished your deliveries?

1037
01:07:45,186 --> 01:07:46,312
Mm.

1038
01:07:46,395 --> 01:07:47,563
Thanks for the help.

1039
01:07:48,230 --> 01:07:49,065
Hm?

1040
01:07:49,148 --> 01:07:52,568
That's great!
They all finally made it home.

1041
01:08:09,835 --> 01:08:12,797
"My dear Violet, are you okay?

1042
01:08:13,589 --> 01:08:16,050
I thought about coming to see you,

1043
01:08:16,133 --> 01:08:18,427
but after talking with Iris,

1044
01:08:18,511 --> 01:08:21,472
we decided to write you a letter instead.

1045
01:08:21,555 --> 01:08:25,643
It might be strange for a Doll
to write to another Doll,

1046
01:08:25,726 --> 01:08:29,105
but we wanted you to know
that we are worried about you.

1047
01:08:29,730 --> 01:08:31,941
And also, that we are here…

1048
01:08:34,026 --> 01:08:35,736
waiting for you."

1049
01:08:37,655 --> 01:08:40,991
You might not feel like coming
back to work at the moment,

1050
01:08:41,075 --> 01:08:43,828
so, please take your time.

1051
01:08:43,911 --> 01:08:49,083
But if something happens,
please don't hesitate to call us.

1052
01:08:49,708 --> 01:08:52,253
Both Iris and I have faith
that you will return.

1053
01:08:57,508 --> 01:09:00,344
Also, someone named Spencer came in,

1054
01:09:00,427 --> 01:09:02,596
asking for you to write a letter for him.

1055
01:09:03,472 --> 01:09:07,184
He said he wanted to send a message
to thank his younger sister.

1056
01:09:08,477 --> 01:09:10,688
And to apologize.

1057
01:09:11,480 --> 01:09:14,525
He tells us he wants you to write it.

1058
01:09:14,608 --> 01:09:16,902
He insists that it has to be you.

1059
01:09:23,742 --> 01:09:25,911
Is this to your satisfaction?

1060
01:09:25,995 --> 01:09:26,954
Yes.

1061
01:09:28,497 --> 01:09:30,583
It's actually a little embarrassing,

1062
01:09:30,666 --> 01:09:32,793
sending a letter to your sister,

1063
01:09:32,877 --> 01:09:36,755
but I just landed a new job
and I owe it to her.

1064
01:09:38,966 --> 01:09:41,844
She helped me decide to start over again.

1065
01:09:44,889 --> 01:09:48,184
Sorry about this.
Having to come all the way here.

1066
01:09:49,185 --> 01:09:51,604
I heard that you were taking
some time off work.

1067
01:09:51,687 --> 01:09:54,064
My coworkers told me of your request…

1068
01:09:55,399 --> 01:09:56,567
through a letter.

1069
01:09:57,193 --> 01:10:01,197
It was the very first letter
I'd ever received.

1070
01:10:02,448 --> 01:10:04,575
And it helped me understand.

1071
01:10:05,910 --> 01:10:09,747
I see how special it is
to receive a letter.

1072
01:10:10,414 --> 01:10:11,540
Oh.

1073
01:10:12,333 --> 01:10:14,585
I think Luculia
will be very happy.

1074
01:10:17,129 --> 01:10:18,130
Thank you.

1075
01:10:45,115 --> 01:10:45,991
Hm?

1076
01:11:27,491 --> 01:11:30,119
One fitting of that name.

1077
01:11:36,709 --> 01:11:37,876
A name…

1078
01:11:38,794 --> 01:11:39,920
that is suitable.

1079
01:12:01,191 --> 01:12:02,234
Huh?

1080
01:12:05,904 --> 01:12:06,739
Oh.

1081
01:12:07,448 --> 01:12:09,116
It is just as you said.

1082
01:12:09,199 --> 01:12:11,869
I had burns all over my body.

1083
01:12:14,913 --> 01:12:15,914
Is it okay?

1084
01:12:16,915 --> 01:12:17,833
Huh?

1085
01:12:18,542 --> 01:12:19,418
So, do I…

1086
01:12:20,461 --> 01:12:23,839
do I have any right to be a Doll?

1087
01:12:24,715 --> 01:12:26,717
-Oh.
-Do I…

1088
01:12:27,551 --> 01:12:29,678
Do I have any right to live?

1089
01:12:40,481 --> 01:12:42,066
You can't erase the past.

1090
01:12:48,906 --> 01:12:49,740
Although…

1091
01:13:22,523 --> 01:13:23,357
Just know…

1092
01:13:26,527 --> 01:13:29,238
everything you've done
as an Auto Memories Doll…

1093
01:13:31,990 --> 01:13:33,784
won't disappear either,

1094
01:13:34,535 --> 01:13:35,828
Violet Evergarden.

1095
01:13:35,911 --> 01:13:36,829
VIOLET EVERGARDEN

1096
01:13:37,413 --> 01:13:39,415
What do you want to do today?

1097
01:13:39,915 --> 01:13:41,291
I don't know.

1098
01:13:42,292 --> 01:13:44,461
Playing house is a little boring.

1099
01:13:45,254 --> 01:13:46,463
Yeah.

1100
01:13:47,214 --> 01:13:50,300
I wonder when Mom's visitors
are going to leave.

1101
01:13:51,802 --> 01:13:54,054
They should go home already.

1102
01:13:55,264 --> 01:13:57,516
Yeah. Hm.

1103
01:13:58,642 --> 01:13:59,476
Huh?

1104
01:14:04,314 --> 01:14:05,732
What's that?

1105
01:14:11,280 --> 01:14:14,032
I saw a doll walking down the path.

1106
01:14:15,701 --> 01:14:18,036
A really big doll.

1107
01:14:20,205 --> 01:14:23,625
For some reason,
I felt like she was something bad.

1108
01:14:26,462 --> 01:14:28,130
Mom! Mom!

1109
01:14:28,213 --> 01:14:29,506
Oh, Miss Ann.

1110
01:14:29,590 --> 01:14:31,508
I see what you're saying, but…

1111
01:14:31,592 --> 01:14:33,051
It's important to do.

1112
01:14:33,135 --> 01:14:35,345
-Yes, but--
-Hey, Mommy!

1113
01:14:35,429 --> 01:14:36,805
Oh, Ann.

1114
01:14:36,889 --> 01:14:39,850
Haven't I told you that you need to knock
before entering a room?

1115
01:14:40,851 --> 01:14:41,685
Uh…

1116
01:14:42,311 --> 01:14:44,563
And to give a proper greeting.

1117
01:14:48,192 --> 01:14:49,485
Welcome to our home.

1118
01:14:50,194 --> 01:14:52,779
-Pardon me, Mother.
-My…

1119
01:14:52,863 --> 01:14:53,989
That's much better.

1120
01:14:55,532 --> 01:14:56,950
Now then, what is it?

1121
01:14:59,077 --> 01:15:01,997
Don't tell me
you found another strange bug?

1122
01:15:02,080 --> 01:15:05,292
-If you did, please don't show me.
-It's not a bug!

1123
01:15:05,876 --> 01:15:07,503
I saw a doll coming to our house!

1124
01:15:07,586 --> 01:15:08,754
A doll?

1125
01:15:09,379 --> 01:15:10,380
Madam.

1126
01:15:11,590 --> 01:15:13,383
She has finally arrived.

1127
01:15:14,384 --> 01:15:16,887
Oh, you mean that Doll.

1128
01:15:16,970 --> 01:15:18,972
That appointment was today, wasn't it?

1129
01:15:19,056 --> 01:15:20,557
Please show her in, Ellis.

1130
01:15:20,641 --> 01:15:22,643
-Of course, madam.
-Wait a second!

1131
01:15:22,726 --> 01:15:25,521
I'm very sorry, but I think
we'll have to do this another time.

1132
01:15:25,604 --> 01:15:26,647
But hold on,

1133
01:15:26,730 --> 01:15:28,649
what are you going to do
with this mansion?

1134
01:15:29,608 --> 01:15:31,652
She can't live here on her own.

1135
01:15:31,735 --> 01:15:33,195
That's why we offered to--

1136
01:15:33,278 --> 01:15:35,614
We'll discuss it next time.

1137
01:15:35,697 --> 01:15:36,990
Wai-- Wait!

1138
01:15:47,125 --> 01:15:49,127
-Ann.
-Huh?

1139
01:15:49,711 --> 01:15:51,505
Be a good girl for me, okay?

1140
01:15:54,883 --> 01:15:56,510
So sorry to have kept you waiting.

1141
01:15:56,593 --> 01:15:59,763
And thank you for coming
all the way out here like this.

1142
01:15:59,846 --> 01:16:01,139
It was no trouble.

1143
01:16:01,223 --> 01:16:03,100
Wow, she can talk!

1144
01:16:05,185 --> 01:16:08,021
If it is your wish,
I will travel anywhere to meet you.

1145
01:16:08,105 --> 01:16:09,856
Auto Memories Doll at your service.

1146
01:16:09,940 --> 01:16:11,692
You're a doll! I knew it!

1147
01:16:11,775 --> 01:16:12,609
Ann!

1148
01:16:13,360 --> 01:16:15,279
-I'm sorry about that.
-It's fine.

1149
01:16:17,823 --> 01:16:19,616
I am Violet Evergarden.

1150
01:16:20,993 --> 01:16:24,496
Please, have a seat.
Would you like some tea?

1151
01:16:30,210 --> 01:16:32,129
I hope you find it to your liking.

1152
01:16:32,212 --> 01:16:34,673
-Please go ahead.
-Thank you.

1153
01:16:35,465 --> 01:16:36,842
Oh. Oh?

1154
01:16:38,510 --> 01:16:39,845
She drank it!

1155
01:16:40,429 --> 01:16:42,723
-What happens to the tea?
-Ann.

1156
01:16:43,390 --> 01:16:46,977
It will eventually be expelled
from my body and return to the earth.

1157
01:16:48,020 --> 01:16:50,397
Ann, please don't be rude.

1158
01:16:51,898 --> 01:16:52,941
Shall we begin?

1159
01:16:53,525 --> 01:16:57,321
I understand that I have been hired
for a seven-day period. Is that right?

1160
01:16:58,155 --> 01:17:00,407
That's right,
and I'd like to start right away.

1161
01:17:00,991 --> 01:17:02,284
All right, I understand.

1162
01:17:02,367 --> 01:17:04,119
Where is it
that you would like us to work?

1163
01:17:04,828 --> 01:17:08,665
Well, how about we go into the sunroom?
It's always nice and bright in there.

1164
01:17:08,749 --> 01:17:10,292
What are you doing?

1165
01:17:10,375 --> 01:17:13,337
Our guest came here today
to help me write a letter.

1166
01:17:13,920 --> 01:17:16,423
But how come?
I would've written a letter for you.

1167
01:17:16,506 --> 01:17:19,593
Thanks, but you don't know how to spell
some of the hard words.

1168
01:17:19,676 --> 01:17:21,053
I can write it!

1169
01:17:21,136 --> 01:17:22,220
I'm sure you can.

1170
01:17:22,304 --> 01:17:24,264
But Miss Violet is very well-known

1171
01:17:24,348 --> 01:17:26,725
for the wonderful letters
that she writes for people.

1172
01:17:28,018 --> 01:17:29,394
Who is the letter to?

1173
01:17:30,103 --> 01:17:31,396
The letter's for…

1174
01:17:32,105 --> 01:17:34,524
somebody who's very far away.

1175
01:17:34,608 --> 01:17:36,818
-Far away?
-Yes.

1176
01:17:37,486 --> 01:17:39,529
It's a very important letter.

1177
01:17:39,613 --> 01:17:41,657
So please don't interrupt us, all right?

1178
01:17:42,240 --> 01:17:43,825
Shall we, Miss Violet?

1179
01:17:44,368 --> 01:17:45,410
Understood.

1180
01:17:47,496 --> 01:17:48,372
Hmp.

1181
01:17:50,666 --> 01:17:53,710
I have brought my own typewriter to use.

1182
01:17:53,794 --> 01:17:55,545
I see. That's fine with me.

1183
01:17:55,629 --> 01:17:57,172
All right, then let's begin.

1184
01:17:59,216 --> 01:18:01,635
I knew there was something bad about her.

1185
01:18:07,808 --> 01:18:10,644
You see? She really is a doll.

1186
01:18:14,648 --> 01:18:15,524
Madam!

1187
01:18:22,948 --> 01:18:25,158
Mom, are you okay?

1188
01:18:25,784 --> 01:18:27,285
I'm just fine, dear.

1189
01:18:27,869 --> 01:18:29,371
I'll be better soon, all right?

1190
01:18:30,247 --> 01:18:31,248
You will?

1191
01:18:34,376 --> 01:18:35,419
I promise.

1192
01:18:36,670 --> 01:18:40,298
I know!
I can sing you a lullaby if you want!

1193
01:18:41,299 --> 01:18:42,509
That's very sweet.

1194
01:18:42,592 --> 01:18:45,512
But grownups don't need lullabies
to help them sleep.

1195
01:18:45,595 --> 01:18:46,638
Oh.

1196
01:18:48,140 --> 01:18:50,142
Then can I sleep here with you?

1197
01:18:50,225 --> 01:18:51,226
Oh.

1198
01:18:51,309 --> 01:18:54,271
But I thought you were too big
to take naps anymore.

1199
01:18:54,354 --> 01:18:55,856
It's okay for just today.

1200
01:18:57,065 --> 01:19:00,986
Well, instead, dear,
I'd rather you go entertain our visitor.

1201
01:19:01,570 --> 01:19:03,029
I hate visitors.

1202
01:19:03,613 --> 01:19:05,991
They all try to take you away from me.

1203
01:19:07,159 --> 01:19:07,993
Oh.

1204
01:19:09,745 --> 01:19:11,246
I'm sorry, Ann.

1205
01:19:12,998 --> 01:19:15,542
But please, it's just for seven days.

1206
01:19:15,625 --> 01:19:18,420
So be a good girl for me. All right?

1207
01:19:19,379 --> 01:19:20,297
Hm.

1208
01:19:24,384 --> 01:19:27,763
My mother said she's going to be resting
for a little while.

1209
01:19:28,430 --> 01:19:29,598
I see.

1210
01:19:31,266 --> 01:19:33,185
She's just a little sleepy.

1211
01:19:34,311 --> 01:19:39,232
During that time, I told her
that I would entertain you instead.

1212
01:19:41,401 --> 01:19:43,487
I actually hate visitors,

1213
01:19:44,571 --> 01:19:46,615
but you're a doll, so it's okay.

1214
01:19:47,824 --> 01:19:49,451
What are we going to do?

1215
01:19:49,534 --> 01:19:50,452
Mm.

1216
01:19:51,077 --> 01:19:55,665
Well, I guess we could talk or play,
or something like that, you know.

1217
01:19:55,749 --> 01:19:58,460
-That is outside my expertise.
-Huh?

1218
01:19:59,294 --> 01:20:00,837
However,

1219
01:20:01,421 --> 01:20:03,215
if it is only for a little while…

1220
01:20:05,467 --> 01:20:08,553
-Then let's play with my doll!
-Okay.

1221
01:20:14,851 --> 01:20:18,814
A doll playing with another doll,
that's so funny!

1222
01:20:20,482 --> 01:20:21,858
What is it that I do with this?

1223
01:20:22,484 --> 01:20:25,946
Oh, well, you just have to talk to her
or take care of her, obviously.

1224
01:20:26,029 --> 01:20:28,073
The first thing to do is say hello.

1225
01:20:29,407 --> 01:20:30,492
Hello there!

1226
01:20:32,035 --> 01:20:33,119
Hello there.

1227
01:20:34,246 --> 01:20:36,164
Oh, hello.

1228
01:20:39,292 --> 01:20:42,295
Oh! The doll was the one who said that!

1229
01:20:43,213 --> 01:20:44,422
Oh, I see.

1230
01:20:45,215 --> 01:20:46,383
I understand then.

1231
01:20:46,466 --> 01:20:48,677
Oh, right! I forgot that you're a doll,

1232
01:20:48,760 --> 01:20:51,471
so, you've never actually played
with one that's just like you,

1233
01:20:51,555 --> 01:20:52,639
isn't that right?

1234
01:20:52,722 --> 01:20:53,849
No, I--

1235
01:20:53,932 --> 01:20:55,475
That's okay. I'll teach you how!

1236
01:20:55,559 --> 01:20:58,395
First, you and I are gonna go play house.

1237
01:20:58,478 --> 01:21:00,397
I have a table for us in the yard.

1238
01:21:00,480 --> 01:21:02,649
Excuse me, your room is ready, ma'am.

1239
01:21:02,732 --> 01:21:04,901
I'd be glad to show you to it if you like.

1240
01:21:04,985 --> 01:21:05,902
Thank you.

1241
01:21:07,445 --> 01:21:09,030
You will have to excuse me.

1242
01:21:09,114 --> 01:21:10,240
Oh.

1243
01:21:11,533 --> 01:21:13,326
Your room is on the second floor.

1244
01:21:22,294 --> 01:21:24,337
I wonder what they're talking about.

1245
01:21:27,632 --> 01:21:30,343
Oh! Ellis!

1246
01:21:31,094 --> 01:21:34,764
-I can take that out!
-Oh, no. You certainly may not.

1247
01:21:34,848 --> 01:21:36,933
This is my job after all.

1248
01:21:37,017 --> 01:21:39,019
Please don't take it from me.

1249
01:21:40,270 --> 01:21:41,146
Ah!

1250
01:21:41,855 --> 01:21:44,608
Why does life
have to be so unfair all the time?

1251
01:22:06,880 --> 01:22:09,299
"Then, the thief was surprised.

1252
01:22:09,382 --> 01:22:11,301
'Ah!' He yelled.

1253
01:22:11,885 --> 01:22:13,553
And then, he ran away for good."

1254
01:22:14,512 --> 01:22:18,058
Did you know that you are really good
at reading stories to someone?

1255
01:22:19,142 --> 01:22:20,727
Violet!

1256
01:22:22,270 --> 01:22:25,231
What are you supposed to do
if bread is really hard

1257
01:22:25,315 --> 01:22:26,942
and can't be eaten?

1258
01:22:27,692 --> 01:22:29,778
You could put it in soup to soften it.

1259
01:22:30,779 --> 01:22:33,323
Violet! Violet!

1260
01:22:33,949 --> 01:22:37,744
Until my mom comes out here,
let's do riddles and dance together

1261
01:22:37,827 --> 01:22:40,455
and play house and catch bugs.
Do you want to?

1262
01:22:40,538 --> 01:22:41,581
-Miss Ann.
-Huh?

1263
01:22:41,665 --> 01:22:44,167
Please tell me the order of priority.

1264
01:22:49,255 --> 01:22:50,507
So, what do you think?

1265
01:22:51,758 --> 01:22:55,553
-I think it's very good.
-Then, I'll continue this way.

1266
01:22:56,763 --> 01:22:57,764
Thank you.

1267
01:23:03,144 --> 01:23:06,064
-Ann?
-Oh, I'm sorry!

1268
01:23:06,147 --> 01:23:10,443
Uh, I was thinking of having Violet
tie a ribbon in my hair.

1269
01:23:10,527 --> 01:23:13,571
All right, fine. Perhaps, a little later.

1270
01:23:13,655 --> 01:23:17,492
Madam, would you allow me
to have a short break?

1271
01:23:17,575 --> 01:23:18,660
Huh?

1272
01:23:18,743 --> 01:23:21,538
I believe Miss Ann
would appreciate it now.

1273
01:23:23,999 --> 01:23:26,042
There you are, Miss Ann.

1274
01:23:27,669 --> 01:23:31,798
You're not the person I actually wanted
to tie the ribbon in my hair.

1275
01:23:32,507 --> 01:23:35,635
-I know.
-I really wanted my mom to do it.

1276
01:23:37,137 --> 01:23:40,056
-I know.
-And she's the one I want to read with,

1277
01:23:40,140 --> 01:23:42,392
and do riddles and play house with.

1278
01:23:42,475 --> 01:23:45,061
But I know my Mom doesn't like bugs.

1279
01:23:45,687 --> 01:23:49,399
Would you stop taking away my time
with my mom, Violet?

1280
01:23:49,482 --> 01:23:51,109
Just a few more days.

1281
01:23:51,192 --> 01:23:54,487
Then you have to tell my mom
it's okay for me to be there

1282
01:23:54,571 --> 01:23:56,072
when you're writing the letter for her!

1283
01:23:56,156 --> 01:23:57,824
I just want to be near her!

1284
01:23:58,408 --> 01:24:02,120
All I want is to be close
and squeeze her hand. Will you?

1285
01:24:03,121 --> 01:24:05,915
I am terribly sorry,
I cannot do that.

1286
01:24:05,999 --> 01:24:07,000
Why not?

1287
01:24:07,751 --> 01:24:09,044
I'm sorry, Miss Ann.

1288
01:24:09,836 --> 01:24:12,255
But unfortunately,
I must be getting back now.

1289
01:24:19,637 --> 01:24:21,556
Do you think
we'll be able to finish today?

1290
01:24:21,639 --> 01:24:24,309
Yes, if we continue at this pace.

1291
01:24:24,392 --> 01:24:26,311
Madam, if you would, please.

1292
01:24:27,312 --> 01:24:28,146
Madam?

1293
01:24:29,981 --> 01:24:33,109
I'll be okay. I just…

1294
01:24:33,193 --> 01:24:34,569
Oh!

1295
01:24:34,652 --> 01:24:35,570
Madam!

1296
01:24:37,530 --> 01:24:39,866
-I'll be all right.
-But…

1297
01:24:39,949 --> 01:24:42,452
No. Please, continue.

1298
01:24:42,535 --> 01:24:45,080
-Stop! That's enough!
-No, Miss Ann!

1299
01:24:45,163 --> 01:24:47,373
-Mom! That's enough!
-Ann.

1300
01:24:48,625 --> 01:24:52,003
I'm okay, really.
So please, go play in the yard.

1301
01:24:54,547 --> 01:24:57,759
But why? Why are you writing this letter?

1302
01:24:57,842 --> 01:25:01,471
Who is it for?
Daddy isn't even with us anymore!

1303
01:25:01,554 --> 01:25:03,223
It's a very important letter.

1304
01:25:03,306 --> 01:25:06,476
It's probably for someone
I don't know, isn't it?

1305
01:25:06,559 --> 01:25:08,812
Someone who doesn't even visit you!

1306
01:25:08,895 --> 01:25:11,856
There isn't anyone
who really cares about you anyway!

1307
01:25:11,940 --> 01:25:13,066
No one!

1308
01:25:19,155 --> 01:25:21,908
Is this letter more important
than I am, Mom?

1309
01:25:25,495 --> 01:25:27,997
There's nothing more important
than you, darling.

1310
01:25:28,748 --> 01:25:30,750
You're such a liar.

1311
01:25:30,834 --> 01:25:32,418
I would never lie to you.

1312
01:25:34,003 --> 01:25:36,673
You are! You're not getting better at all!

1313
01:25:36,756 --> 01:25:38,508
And you told me
you were going to get better.

1314
01:25:38,591 --> 01:25:39,843
You promised me!

1315
01:25:39,926 --> 01:25:41,261
That's right.

1316
01:25:41,344 --> 01:25:43,012
I already know, okay?

1317
01:25:43,805 --> 01:25:44,764
I know that if…

1318
01:25:44,848 --> 01:25:47,767
If you're gone,
then I'm gonna be left here all alone!

1319
01:25:50,520 --> 01:25:54,107
Just how much longer
will I be able to be with you?

1320
01:25:56,442 --> 01:25:58,319
If I'm going to be all alone anyway,

1321
01:25:58,403 --> 01:26:00,655
then can you please
stop writing some letter

1322
01:26:00,738 --> 01:26:02,448
and spend time with me now!

1323
01:26:02,532 --> 01:26:04,450
Please, Mom! Please!

1324
01:26:04,534 --> 01:26:06,327
Please, Mom!

1325
01:26:06,411 --> 01:26:08,246
-I just want…
-Miss Ann.

1326
01:26:08,329 --> 01:26:10,123
…to spend time with you!

1327
01:26:14,961 --> 01:26:16,379
Miss Ann! Wait!

1328
01:26:47,660 --> 01:26:48,661
Miss Ann.

1329
01:26:50,163 --> 01:26:51,748
I want to reassure you

1330
01:26:51,831 --> 01:26:55,084
that the time I spend with your mother
is for a good cause.

1331
01:26:55,168 --> 01:26:59,088
So, please, I would ask you
not to be angry with your mother.

1332
01:27:00,340 --> 01:27:02,175
But… But…

1333
01:27:02,759 --> 01:27:05,720
It is only natural
that this is painful for you.

1334
01:27:05,803 --> 01:27:10,141
You had to accept your mother's sickness
at such a young age.

1335
01:27:10,934 --> 01:27:12,810
You are very admirable.

1336
01:27:12,894 --> 01:27:14,187
I'm not.

1337
01:27:16,231 --> 01:27:17,357
No, I'm not!

1338
01:27:18,483 --> 01:27:19,734
I…

1339
01:27:19,817 --> 01:27:22,570
I made Mom… I made her cry!

1340
01:27:23,238 --> 01:27:24,113
You didn't.

1341
01:27:24,197 --> 01:27:26,491
In fact, you are a very kind person.

1342
01:27:26,574 --> 01:27:28,243
-I'm not.
-You are.

1343
01:27:28,326 --> 01:27:32,538
I'm not! I'm not! I'm not!

1344
01:27:32,622 --> 01:27:35,375
My mom got sick because I'm a bad girl!

1345
01:27:37,085 --> 01:27:38,461
That's not what she said.

1346
01:27:39,087 --> 01:27:41,631
It is! It is!

1347
01:27:42,715 --> 01:27:46,261
There is nothing…
There is nothing that can be done.

1348
01:27:46,344 --> 01:27:47,720
You're wrong!

1349
01:27:47,804 --> 01:27:49,681
It's just like my arms

1350
01:27:49,764 --> 01:27:54,227
can never be soft and warm
like the way yours will always be.

1351
01:27:57,855 --> 01:27:59,857
There is nothing that can be done.

1352
01:28:06,281 --> 01:28:08,866
Mom! Mom!

1353
01:28:13,121 --> 01:28:15,331
Why is she writing a letter?

1354
01:28:16,457 --> 01:28:18,918
People have feelings
they want to express to others.

1355
01:28:20,086 --> 01:28:21,129
Who cares?

1356
01:28:22,714 --> 01:28:24,757
They don't need to.

1357
01:28:28,553 --> 01:28:33,433
There is no such thing as a letter that
doesn't deserve to be delivered, Miss Ann.

1358
01:28:45,945 --> 01:28:50,158
Then, the day came
when the doll who visited us

1359
01:28:50,241 --> 01:28:53,161
had finished writing the letters
and it was time to say goodbye.

1360
01:29:05,256 --> 01:29:06,090
Violet!

1361
01:29:07,592 --> 01:29:08,509
Hm?

1362
01:29:15,892 --> 01:29:17,518
-Thank you, Miss Ann.
-Huh?

1363
01:29:20,813 --> 01:29:22,023
It's warm.

1364
01:29:25,902 --> 01:29:27,070
Wait, are you…

1365
01:29:28,946 --> 01:29:31,032
Then what about the tea you drank?

1366
01:29:31,115 --> 01:29:31,949
As I said,

1367
01:29:32,658 --> 01:29:36,204
I will eventually expel it from my body
and it will return to the earth.

1368
01:29:43,961 --> 01:29:45,963
She wasn't a doll after all.

1369
01:29:47,131 --> 01:29:49,717
And she wasn't something bad either.

1370
01:29:50,885 --> 01:29:52,720
She was very kind.

1371
01:29:54,305 --> 01:29:59,018
I really wish that I could have read
the letters she wrote.

1372
01:30:00,186 --> 01:30:02,438
I wonder who they were for.

1373
01:30:03,147 --> 01:30:03,981
Ann.

1374
01:30:04,690 --> 01:30:07,318
Come, dear. Come inside and have some tea.

1375
01:30:08,611 --> 01:30:11,364
Mom, let's play with my doll!

1376
01:30:11,447 --> 01:30:13,825
-Okay.
-Then we can read books

1377
01:30:13,908 --> 01:30:16,160
-and play house and…
-All right.

1378
01:30:27,672 --> 01:30:28,506
Ann.

1379
01:30:33,761 --> 01:30:34,595
Ann.

1380
01:30:40,059 --> 01:30:41,394
My sweet girl.

1381
01:31:02,290 --> 01:31:03,207
Ann.

1382
01:31:08,379 --> 01:31:09,213
Dear Ann.

1383
01:31:09,881 --> 01:31:12,508
Happy eighth birthday.

1384
01:31:12,592 --> 01:31:15,386
There might be many sad things happening,

1385
01:31:15,470 --> 01:31:18,598
and you might be feeling
really overwhelmed right now.

1386
01:31:18,681 --> 01:31:20,600
But don't give up hope.

1387
01:31:20,683 --> 01:31:24,770
I know you may be sad
and feel like crying sometimes,

1388
01:31:24,854 --> 01:31:27,148
but please, don't ever forget,

1389
01:31:27,231 --> 01:31:30,067
your mother loves you very much.

1390
01:31:30,151 --> 01:31:31,360
Even now.

1391
01:31:33,446 --> 01:31:34,947
Dear Ann,

1392
01:31:35,031 --> 01:31:37,200
happy tenth birthday.

1393
01:31:37,283 --> 01:31:40,411
I'm sure you've grown up quite a lot.

1394
01:31:40,495 --> 01:31:45,124
But I imagine you still love reading
and dancing like you always did.

1395
01:31:45,958 --> 01:31:49,128
Perhaps you moved on
from riddles and bugs?

1396
01:31:52,423 --> 01:31:54,759
Happy 18th birthday.

1397
01:31:55,468 --> 01:31:57,512
You're a young lady now.

1398
01:31:58,554 --> 01:32:00,223
Have you fallen in love?

1399
01:32:01,307 --> 01:32:04,018
I might not be able to help you with that,

1400
01:32:04,101 --> 01:32:06,646
but I'm sure whoever you choose

1401
01:32:06,729 --> 01:32:08,481
is a wonderful person.

1402
01:32:14,904 --> 01:32:17,156
Happy birthday, Ann.

1403
01:32:17,240 --> 01:32:21,536
You're already 20 years old now.
That's amazing.

1404
01:32:21,619 --> 01:32:25,414
But remember, that even adults
are allowed to complain sometimes.

1405
01:32:26,207 --> 01:32:30,461
Whenever you're feeling down,
remember that I am with you.

1406
01:32:32,255 --> 01:32:33,089
Ann.

1407
01:32:35,508 --> 01:32:41,180
I will always,
always be watching over you.

1408
01:33:01,367 --> 01:33:02,535
Great work, Violet.

1409
01:33:03,369 --> 01:33:04,537
You did so many.

1410
01:33:04,620 --> 01:33:07,582
These letters are to be delivered
to Ann Magnolia

1411
01:33:07,665 --> 01:33:09,417
over the course of the next 50 years.

1412
01:33:10,001 --> 01:33:11,919
You wrote 50 letters?

1413
01:33:12,003 --> 01:33:14,630
It was the first extended trip
you've taken in a while.

1414
01:33:14,714 --> 01:33:15,923
Did you handle it okay?

1415
01:33:16,007 --> 01:33:19,385
-There was no problem.
-But this is great.

1416
01:33:19,969 --> 01:33:22,847
She's going to look forward
to these coming every year.

1417
01:33:22,930 --> 01:33:24,599
Yes, but…

1418
01:33:26,934 --> 01:33:28,519
…by the time they arrive,

1419
01:33:28,603 --> 01:33:30,313
her mother will already be…

1420
01:33:31,480 --> 01:33:33,816
She's still so little.

1421
01:33:35,359 --> 01:33:36,611
She gets so lonely.

1422
01:33:37,862 --> 01:33:41,490
And Ann's mother will be leaving
her precious daughter alone.

1423
01:33:43,451 --> 01:33:44,785
She'll be left all alone…

1424
01:33:45,911 --> 01:33:47,246
in that mansion.

1425
01:33:47,872 --> 01:33:48,748
I…

1426
01:33:53,210 --> 01:33:58,466
I… had to hold back my tears
the whole time I was at the mansion.

1427
01:33:59,508 --> 01:34:00,384
I know.

1428
01:34:01,302 --> 01:34:02,637
But, Violet…

1429
01:34:03,888 --> 01:34:04,930
they'll reach her.

1430
01:34:05,765 --> 01:34:07,725
All the letters you wrote for her.

1431
01:34:12,438 --> 01:34:15,566
Don't worry.
No matter where she is, you'll see.

1432
01:34:16,359 --> 01:34:20,696
A LOVED ONE
WILL ALWAYS WATCH OVER YOU

